dgartes_portugal_9958967f7dcb,dgartes_portugal,http://www.dgartes.gov.pt/sites/default/files/avisodeabertura_bv2027.pdf,,Direção-Geral das Artes (DGARTES),"A Direção-Geral das Artes (DGARTES) torna público, através do presente aviso, a abertura do concurso limitado para a apresentação de candidaturas no âmbito do Programa de Apoio a Projetos – Representação Oficial Portuguesa, na 20.ª Exposição Internacional de Arquitetura – La Biennale di Venezia 2027, para seleção do projeto curatorial e expositivo, conforme o disposto no Decreto -Lei n.º 103/2017, de 24 de agosto, na redação atual e no Regulamento dos Programas de Apoio às Artes aprovado em anexo à Portaria n.º 345-A/2026/1, de 14 de agosto, nos termos seguintes:",Arquitetura,concurso limitado,Itália,Veneza,"1. Dotação financeira disponível: 1. 500.000,00€ (quinhentos mil euros), com a seguinte distribuição anual: a) 2026 – 300.000,00€ (trezentos mil euros); b) 2027 – até 200.000,00€ (duzentos mil euros). 2. O montante máximo a ser solicitado em candidatura é de 497.000,00€ (quatrocentos e noventa e sete mil euros).",,,pt,Programa de Apoio a Projetos – Representação Oficial Portuguesa na 20.ª Exposição Internacional de Arquitetura – La Biennale di Venezia 2027,"E. Destinatários: Nos termos do Aviso n.º 15360/2026/2, de 22 de junho, foram selecionadas as seguintes propostas a convidar para integrar o concurso limitado: − Analog Twins, de Alice Clanet-Hallard, Edgar Brito, Francisco Lobo e Romea Muryn − Mãos ao Chão (Hands to the Ground), de Joanna Alice Helm, Remígio Van Eyes Chilaule e Samuel de Brito Gonçalves − Matéria Viva — Os materiais da construção portuguesa e o saber que resiste, de Helena Botelho",Support Program for Projects – Official Portuguese Representation at the 20th International Architecture Exhibition – La Biennale di Venezia 2027,"E. Recipients: Under Notice No. 15360/2026/2, of 22 June, the following proposals were selected to be invited to take part in the restricted competition: − Analog Twins, by Alice Clanet-Hallard, Edgar Brito, Francisco Lobo and Romea Muryn − Mãos ao Chão (Hands to the Ground), by Joanna Alice Helm, Remígio Van Eyes Chilaule and Samuel de Brito Gonçalves − Matéria Viva — Os materiais da construção portuguesa e o saber que resiste, by Helena Botelho",6 de outubro de 2026,2026-10-06,2026-09-23 12:37:21.058425+00:00
dgartes_portugal_c966cce2ccf0,dgartes_portugal,https://www.dgartes.gov.pt/pt/apoio/10166,https://apoios.dgartes.gov.pt/,Direção-Geral das Artes (DGARTES),"a abertura do concurso limitado para a apresentação de candidaturas no âmbito do Programa de Apoio a Projetos – Representação Oficial Portuguesa, na 20.ª Exposição Internacional de Arquitetura – La Biennale di Venezia 2027, para seleção do projeto curatorial e expositivo",Arquitetura,concurso limitado,Portugal,Lisboa,Apoio Financeiro: €500.000,,,pt,[Concurso Limitado] Programa de Apoio a Projetos - Representação Oficial Portuguesa na 20.ª Exposição Internacional de Arquitetura - La Biennale di Venezia 2027,"a apresentação de candidaturas no âmbito do Programa de Apoio a Projetos – Representação Oficial Portuguesa, na 20.ª Exposição Internacional de Arquitetura – La Biennale di Venezia 2027, para seleção do projeto curatorial e expositivo",[Limited Competition] Project Support Program - Official Portuguese Representation at the 20th International Architecture Exhibition - La Biennale di Venezia 2027,"applications under the Project Support Program – Official Portuguese Representation, for the 20th International Architecture Exhibition – La Biennale di Venezia 2027, for the selection of the curatorial and exhibition project",às 17h59m59s do dia 6 de outubro de 2026,2026-09-24,2026-09-23 12:37:22.307414+00:00
dgartes_portugal_b0e4ca961b8e,dgartes_portugal,http://www.dgartes.gov.pt/sites/default/files/aviso_abertura_orquestra_regional_alentejo_2026.pdf,,DGARTES,Concurso para criação de Orquestra Regional do Alentejo,música erudita,Concurso,Portugal,Alentejo,"O montante global disponível é de 1.620.000 € (um milhão seiscentos e vinte mil euros ), a atribuir por um período de dois anos: 2027: 810.000 € 2028: 810.000 €",,,pt,Concurso para criação de Orquestra Regional do Alentejo,"Pessoas coletivas de direito privado sem fins lucrativos, com sede na região do Alentejo , doravante designadas entidades promotoras das orquestras regionais.
Não são admitidas ao procedimento concursal as fundações privadas ou as fundações públicas de direito privado que tenham outro tipo de financiamento continuado, assegurado pelo programa orçamental da área da cultura, bem como empresas do setor público empresarial do Estado. 
2. Estão impedidas de apresentar candidaturas ao presente programa de apoio  as entidades beneficiárias de Apoio Sustentado.   

3. Os órgãos sociais das entidades promotoras das orquestras regionais devem incluir  um número mínimo de cinco municípios na circunscrição territorial ( NUTS II) do Alentejo. 
4. Os órgãos sociais podem incluir ainda outros agentes locais ou regionais da região onde se insere a Orquestra Regional, para além do número de municípios mencionados no n.º 3.",Call for the creation of the Alentejo Regional Orchestra,"Private legal entities without profit-making purposes, with headquarters in the Alentejo region, hereinafter referred to as promoting entities of the regional orchestras.
Private foundations or public foundations under private law that have another type of ongoing funding ensured by the budget programme of the culture area, as well as companies of the State public business sector, are not admitted to the competitive procedure.
2. Entities benefiting from Sustained Support are barred from submitting applications to this support programme.

3. The governing bodies of the promoting entities of the regional orchestras must include a minimum number of five municipalities in the territorial circumscription (NUTS II) of Alentejo.
4. The governing bodies may also include other local or regional agents of the region where the Regional Orchestra is located, in addition to the number of municipalities mentioned in point 3.",Conforme aviso publicado na 2.ª série do Diário da República de 15 de julho,2027-07-15,2026-09-23 12:37:23.908569+00:00
dgartes_portugal_cc9be82e728f,dgartes_portugal,https://www.dgartes.gov.pt/pt/apoio/10064,https://www.dgartes.gov.pt/sites/default/files/formulario_concurso_orquestra_regional_alentejo_2026.xlsx,Direção-Geral das Artes (DGARTES),"a abertura de concurso para criação da Orquestra Regional do Alentejo, com o montante financeiro global disponível de 1.620.000,00 € (um milhão seiscentos e vinte mil euros), com a seguinte distribuição anual: 2027: 810.000,00 € (oitocentos e dez mil euros); 2028: 810.000,00 € (oitocentos e dez mil euros).",Artes / música,concurso,Portugal,null,"com o montante financeiro global disponível de 1.620.000,00 € (um milhão seiscentos e vinte mil euros), com a seguinte distribuição anual: 2027: 810.000,00 € (oitocentos e dez mil euros); 2028: 810.000,00 € (oitocentos e dez mil euros).",,,pt,CONCURSO PARA CRIAÇÃO DA ORQUESTRA REGIONAL DO ALENTEJO,As candidaturas estão abertas até ao dia 9 de setembro de 2026.,OPEN CALL FOR THE CREATION OF THE ALENTEJO REGIONAL ORCHESTRA,"Applications are open until September 9, 2026.",Novo prazo: a apresentação de candidaturas termina às 17:59:59 do dia 25 de setembro de 2026.,2026-09-23,2026-09-23 12:37:24.916519+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_ad15a329abd7,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/culture-helps-solidarity-%d0%ba%d1%83%d0%bb%d1%8c%d1%82%d1%83%d1%80%d0%b0-%d0%b4%d0%be%d0%bf%d0%be%d0%bc%d0%b0%d0%b3%d0%b0%d1%94-open-call-for-collaboration-grants/second-culture-helps-solidarity-call-for-collaboration-grants/,https://culture-of-solidarity-fund.grantplatform.com/,Culture Helps Solidarity,"Culture Helps Solidarity is launching its second and final call for Collaboration Grants . This call supports international projects that use arts and culture to aid the integration of displaced Ukrainians into host communities, with a strong focus on mental well-being, vulnerable groups, and veterans . The fund prioritises cross-border partnerships between at least one Ukrainian-led organisation (operating in Ukraine or in exile) and at least one organisation based in a Creative Europe country . Grants of up to €20,000 are available for partnerships of two organisations, and up to €30,000 for partnerships involving three or more partners . The projects should foster intercultural dialogue, professional exchange, and long-term solidarity .",arts and culture,Collaboration Grants,,,"Grants of up to €20,000 are available for partnerships of two organisations, and up to €30,000 for partnerships involving three or more partners .",,,en,Second Culture Helps Solidarity call for Collaboration Grants,The fund prioritises cross-border partnerships between at least one Ukrainian-led organisation (operating in Ukraine or in exile) and at least one organisation based in a Creative Europe country .,Second Culture Helps Solidarity call for Collaboration Grants,The fund prioritises cross-border partnerships between at least one Ukrainian-led organisation (operating in Ukraine or in exile) and at least one organisation based in a Creative Europe country .,"November 10, 2026, at 13:00 Amsterdam time / 14:00 Kyiv time",2026-11-10,2026-09-23 12:37:24.930215+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_f1e9b1c26c84,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/second-culture-helps-solidarity-call-for-project-grants/,https://culture-of-solidarity-fund.grantplatform.com/,Culture Helps Solidarity,"The second call for Projects Grants of Culture Helps Solidarity focuses on memory and commemoration projects that work responsibly with the lived experiences of people affected byRussia’s war against Ukraine. The call will support cultural and community-based initiatives that create meaningful forms of remembrance, documentation (both analog and digital), public reflection, and commemoration while respecting the dignity, safety, and agency of thosewhose stories and losses are represented. This call supports small-scale cultural projects that engage with the experiences, memories, and histories of people directly affected by Russia’s war against Ukraine, including but not limited to women veterans, families of the fallen, displaced communities, local residents,people who have experienced loss, captivity, injury, or displacement, and witnesses of wartime events. We invite cultural workers, artists, researchers, community organisers, memory practitioners, and civil society initiatives based in Ukraine and across Europe to develop projects that approach remembrance as a careful, inclusive, and community-led practice. Through artistic, educational, research-based, or participatory formats, projects should create meaningful opportunities for reflection, strengthen local and collective memory across generations, amplify diverse voices, and help people feel seen and heard. Ultimately, the call seeks to support cultural practices that contribute to a more responsible public conversation about theongoing impact and aftermath of Russia’s war against Ukraine, both within Ukraine and across Europe.","cultural, artistic, educational, research-based, or participatory",Project Grants,Ukraine and across Europe,,Project Grants,,,en,Second Culture Helps Solidarity call for Project Grants,"We invite cultural workers, artists, researchers, community organisers, memory practitioners, and civil society initiatives based in Ukraine and across Europe to develop projects that approach remembrance as a careful, inclusive, and community-led practice.",Second Culture Helps Solidarity call for Project Grants,"We invite cultural workers, artists, researchers, community organisers, memory practitioners, and civil society initiatives based in Ukraine and across Europe to develop projects that approach remembrance as a careful, inclusive, and community-led practice.",,,2026-09-23 12:37:24.930266+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_80ce5461aa91,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/new-fellowship-programme-to-research-the-ecf-historical-archives/,https://ecf-fellowship.grantplatform.com/,European Cultural Foundation,"This ECF Fellowship aims to foster new research and creative work engaging with the history of the European Cultural Foundation and the broader role of culture in shaping Europe as a shared space of imagination, cooperation, and solidarity.",research and creative work,Fellowship programme,,Florence,"Academic Research Fellowship includes a grant of €5,000 to support a research stay at the HAEU, including travel, accommodation, and living expenses. Artistic Research Fellowship includes a grant of €10,000 to support a research stay at the HAEU, including travel, accommodation, and living expenses, as well as artistic production.",,,en,New Fellowship Programme to Research the ECF Historical Archives,"Fellows are expected to work substantially with the ECF archival holdings – primarily in English, with significant material in French, German, and Dutch, and additional languages occasionally represented.",New Fellowship Programme to Research the ECF Historical Archives,"Fellows are expected to work substantially with the ECF archival holdings – primarily in English, with significant material in French, German, and Dutch, and additional languages occasionally represented.",30 September 2026 at 17:00 CET,2026-09-30,2026-09-23 12:37:24.938042+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_a246059c820a,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/culture-helps-solidarity-open-call-for-individual-grants-4th-round/,https://qr1.be/8KS5J3,European Cultural Foundation,"The fourth round of Culture Helps Solidarity Individual Grants is now open . The programme offers flexible grants of up to €1,200 to Ukrainian cultural professionals working with displaced people, refugees and other vulnerable communities, including veterans, in Ukraine and across Creative Europe countries. Rather than funding projects, these grants are designed to support the individuals behind the work.",cultural professionals,Individual Grants,Ukraine,,"flexible grants of up to €1,200",,,en,Culture Helps Solidarity: Open Call for Individual Grants (4th Round),"to Ukrainian cultural professionals working with displaced people, refugees and other vulnerable communities, including veterans, in Ukraine and across Creative Europe countries.",Culture Helps Solidarity: Open Call for Individual Grants (4th Round),"to Ukrainian cultural professionals working with displaced people, refugees and other vulnerable communities, including veterans, in Ukraine and across Creative Europe countries.",29 June 2026,2026-06-29,2026-09-23 12:37:24.944339+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_67a05c59b453,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/culture-helps-solidarity-%d0%ba%d1%83%d0%bb%d1%8c%d1%82%d1%83%d1%80%d0%b0-%d0%b4%d0%be%d0%bf%d0%be%d0%bc%d0%b0%d0%b3%d0%b0%d1%94-open-call-for-individual-care-grants-round-2/,https://qr1.be/BXQZDY,European Cultural Foundation,"The call supports Ukrainian cultural workers who need time and resources to focus on well-being, recovery and the conditions needed to continue their cultural work.","artists, cultural practitioners and creative professionals",Individual Care Grants,Ukraine,Kyiv,"Across the programme, more than €1.4 million will support over 200 individuals and organisations, alongside opportunities for learning, mentoring and exchange that strengthen professional capacity and cross-border connection.",,,en,Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Open Call for Individual Care Grants Round 2,"The grants are open to artists, cultural practitioners and creative professionals from Ukraine, whether they remain in the country or are temporarily displaced elsewhere.",Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Open Call for Individual Care Grants Round 2,"The grants are open to artists, cultural practitioners and creative professionals from Ukraine, whether they remain in the country or are temporarily displaced elsewhere.",6 April 2026 at 13:00 (Amsterdam time),2026-04-06,2026-09-23 12:37:24.949138+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_cf66f32bd199,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/culture-helps-solidarity-%d0%ba%d1%83%d0%bb%d1%8c%d1%82%d1%83%d1%80%d0%b0-%d0%b4%d0%be%d0%bf%d0%be%d0%bc%d0%b0%d0%b3%d0%b0%d1%94-%d1%81%d0%be%d0%bb%d1%96%d0%b4%d0%b0%d1%80%d0%bd%d1%96%d1%81%d1%82/,https://qr1.be/93Y8G0,"Insha Osvita in Kyiv, zusa in Berlin, the Veteranka Movement in Kyiv and the European Cultural Foundation in Amsterdam","Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Солідарність is opening a round of Individual Care Grants from 2 to 23 February 2026 to support creative professionals and veterans in maintaining their mental health and wellbeing, helping them sustain the care and cultural work they provide to others. The programme is delivered by Insha Osvita in Kyiv, zusa in Berlin, the Veteranka Movement in Kyiv and the European Cultural Foundation in Amsterdam. Support focuses on personal well-being rather than project delivery. It may include counselling, trauma-informed coaching, restorative care, or participation in cultural and therapeutic activities that help individuals recover balance and resilience.",arts and culture,Individual Care Grants,Ukraine,Kyiv,"Grants of up to €1,200",,,en,Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Солідарність Individual Care Grants Open,"individuals working in arts and culture who support displaced Ukrainians, particularly vulnerable groups such as veterans, and who have themselves been affected by war or displacement.",Culture Helps Solidarity / Культура допомагає: Солідарність Individual Care Grants Open,"individuals working in arts and culture who support displaced Ukrainians, particularly vulnerable groups such as veterans, and who have themselves been affected by war or displacement.",from 2 to 23 February 2026,2026-02-23,2026-09-23 12:37:24.952675+00:00
european_cultural_foundation_7395e3ac9c32,european_cultural_foundation,https://culturalfoundation.eu/open-calls/civitates-media-open-call/,https://civitates-eu.org/funding-opportunity/call-for-proposals-strengthening-independent-public-interest-journalism-in-europe/,Civitates,"Applications are now open for Civitates ’ Media open call for proposals , aimed at supporting independent public interest journalism across Europe. This is an opportunity for non-profit media organizations to secure core funding to strengthen their sustainability, build resilience, and enhance their contributions to a balanced and respectful public dialogue. The call focuses on helping independent media outlets: Strengthen their organizational sustainability and operational stability. Innovate with new business models and editorial strategies. Deepen audience engagement and expand public outreach.",public interest journalism,open call for proposals,Europe,,"Eligible organisations can apply for up to €160,000 in core funding, distributed over two years, to support mid-term goals and operational growth.",,,en,Civitates Media Open Call,"Civitates invites applications from independent media outlets registered in Hungary, Poland, Italy, Spain, Bulgaria, Slovakia, and Croatia.",Civitates Media Open Call,"Civitates invites applications from independent media outlets registered in Hungary, Poland, Italy, Spain, Bulgaria, Slovakia, and Croatia.",,,2026-09-23 12:37:24.952720+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_641becbe2421,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/short-term-conference-and-travel-grant/,,Gulbenkian,"These short-term scholarships enable qualified students, early-career academics and researchers based in Armenia to take part in international conferences, seminars, short courses and research trips abroad related to their field of study. The programme aims to encourage academic exchange and the sharing of knowledge and ideas.",all fields of research,scholarships,Armenia,,"The scholarship amount is fixed; please refer to the table in the Requirements, Criteria and Conditions document for details. All scholarships are awarded and paid in euros.",,"graduate students, early-career academics and researchers",en,Short Term Conference and Travel Scholarships,"Applicants must be: Studying or based in Armenia. Under 35 years old at the time of the application. A Master’s or PhD student, or a researcher from Armenia, wishing to attend international conferences, seminars, short-term courses or undertake research trips related to their field of study.",Short Term Conference and Travel Scholarships,"Applicants must be: Studying or based in Armenia. Under 35 years old at the time of the application. A Master’s or PhD student, or a researcher from Armenia, wishing to attend international conferences, seminars, short-term courses or undertake research trips related to their field of study.",End date 04 Dec 2026 / 23:59 Lisbon time,2026-12-04,2026-09-23 12:37:24.956685+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_9db5c1bb86df,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/visiting-professorships-in-the-humanities/,,Gulbenkian,The Gulbenkian Visiting Professorships in the Humanities aim to strengthen the quality and internationalisation of teaching and research in Portugal by hosting distinguished foreign scholars.,Humanities,Visiting Professorships,Portugal,,"Monthly stipend: €4,000 One-time allowance for travel and relocation: €4,000",,senior researchers with a well-established scientific track record,en,Visiting Professorships in the Humanities,"Only Portuguese Higher Education Institutions (HEIs) are eligible, and the proposed academic activities must take place in Portugal. Applications must be submitted by the professor responsible for coordinating the visit, on behalf of the Portuguese HEI. The visiting professor is not eligible to apply directly.",Visiting Professorships in the Humanities,"Only Portuguese Higher Education Institutions (HEIs) are eligible, and the proposed academic activities must take place in Portugal. Applications must be submitted by the professor responsible for coordinating the visit, on behalf of the Portuguese HEI. The visiting professor is not eligible to apply directly.",30 Sep 2026 / 17:00 Lisbon time,2026-09-30,2026-09-23 12:37:24.963267+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_86e33a273257,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/gulbenkian-new-talents-scholarships/,https://gulbenkian.pt/my/login?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fgulbenkian.pt%2F,Gulbenkian Foundation,"The Gulbenkian New Talents Scholarships programme seeks to identify and support exceptionally talented students and foster their first steps into research in core scientific disciplines such as biology, geology, physics, mathematics and chemistry, as well as in any field of the humanities, arts or social sciences.","biology, geology, physics, mathematics and chemistry, as well as in any field of the humanities, arts or social sciences",scholarships,Portugal,,"The annual scholarship amount is made up of three components: Research and study support – €1,000

Talent development support – €1,500

Supplementary social support – €2,000",,students,en,Gulbenkian New Talents Scholarships,"Applications are open to students who:
Will be enrolled in the 2nd, 3rd or 4th year of a bachelor’s degree or integrated master’s programme, or in the 1st year of a master’s degree, during the 2026/2027 academic year at a higher education institution in Portugal.
Have an average grade of 16.5 or above (on a 20-point scale) in the curricular units completed in the bachelor’s program to date.",Gulbenkian New Talents Scholarships,"Applications are open to students who:
Will be enrolled in the 2nd, 3rd or 4th year of a bachelor’s degree or integrated master’s programme, or in the 1st year of a master’s degree, during the 2026/2027 academic year at a higher education institution in Portugal.
Have an average grade of 16.5 or above (on a 20-point scale) in the curricular units completed in the bachelor’s program to date.",30 Sep 2026 / 15:00,2026-09-30,2026-09-23 12:37:24.973719+00:00
fundacao_gulbenkian_0089a729f2c8,fundacao_gulbenkian,https://gulbenkian.pt/en/bolsas-lista/gulbenkian-merit-scholarships/,,Gulbenkian,These scholarships are intended to support high-potential young students applying for the first year of higher education who demonstrate limited financial resources.,higher education,scholarships,Portugal,Lisbon,"The scholarship amounts to €2,000 per academic year and includes an additional one-time grant of €2,000 for participation in an international mobility period, such as Erasmus or another similar programme offered by each higher education institution.",,young students,en,Gulbenkian Merit scholarships,"Admission grade for higher education equal to or higher than 170 points through the general access and admission competition for the 2026/27 academic year, in the programme in which the applicant is enrolled. Proof of application for a social action grant from the Directorate-General for Higher Education (DGES). In order to enable verification of household income, applying for a DGES grant is a mandatory condition for applying for the Gulbenkian Merit Scholarship, regardless of household income level. Scholarships will only be awarded to selected applicants whose annual per capita income, as verified by the Social Services of the respective higher education institution, does not exceed €14,000. Only applicants to legally recognised Portuguese higher education institutions and duly accredited and registered study programmes will be considered. Applications from holders of a higher education degree will not be accepted.",Gulbenkian Merit scholarships,"Admission grade for higher education equal to or higher than 170 points through the general access and admission competition for the 2026/27 academic year, in the programme in which the applicant is enrolled. Proof of application for a social action grant from the Directorate-General for Higher Education (DGES). In order to enable verification of household income, applying for a DGES grant is a mandatory condition for applying for the Gulbenkian Merit Scholarship, regardless of household income level. Scholarships will only be awarded to selected applicants whose annual per capita income, as verified by the Social Services of the respective higher education institution, does not exceed €14,000. Only applicants to legally recognised Portuguese higher education institutions and duly accredited and registered study programmes will be considered. Applications from holders of a higher education degree will not be accepted.",30 Oct 2026 / 15:00 Lisbon time,2026-10-30,2026-09-23 12:37:24.977840+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_28c59766a0db,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/exhibition-of-danish-art-abroad,https://portal.slks.dk//TAS_Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=7062179a8b2e49e1835fe8c4cd354c60,Danish Arts Foundation,"International Grants for the production, dissemination, and exhibition of contemporary art in Denmark and abroad.",Visual arts,grant,Denmark,,,,,en,Exhibition of Danish Art Abroad,"Who may apply? You can apply if you plan to produce an art piece to be exhibited in Denmark or abroad And You can apply if you shall exhibit and/or promote the work of living visual artists in Denmark or abroad. Is your project interdisciplinary? Find out more about how to apply if your project combines different art forms . The grant does NOT cover: Exhibitions that open before the deadline. Gallery exhibitions: Artists may apply for grants for the production of new works. Other expenses for the exhibition are only covered if the committee assesses them as a special investment by the gallery Permanent works in public space – here defined as art projects that are publicly accessible in a period of more than 12 months. These are funded through other programs. Studio rent Per diem allowance Invitations, meals, etc. in connection with exhibition previews Travel and accommodation for assistants (generally not covered) Travel and accommodation in connection with exhibitions in galleries where the artist has a permanent affiliation Local transport Projects already reviewed by the committee. Costs from previous calendar years.",Exhibition of Danish Art Abroad,"Who may apply? You can apply if you plan to produce an art piece to be exhibited in Denmark or abroad And You can apply if you shall exhibit and/or promote the work of living visual artists in Denmark or abroad. Is your project interdisciplinary? Find out more about how to apply if your project combines different art forms . The grant does NOT cover: Exhibitions that open before the deadline. Gallery exhibitions: Artists may apply for grants for the production of new works. Other expenses for the exhibition are only covered if the committee assesses them as a special investment by the gallery Permanent works in public space – here defined as art projects that are publicly accessible in a period of more than 12 months. These are funded through other programs. Studio rent Per diem allowance Invitations, meals, etc. in connection with exhibition previews Travel and accommodation for assistants (generally not covered) Travel and accommodation in connection with exhibitions in galleries where the artist has a permanent affiliation Local transport Projects already reviewed by the committee. Costs from previous calendar years.","24.09.2026, 2:00 PM",2026-09-24,2026-09-23 12:37:24.987219+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_83c3b68dac03,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/visual-arts-international-research-programme,https://portal.slks.dk/Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=14cde2fa1f14488ea90a43972c3a47d5,Danish Arts Foundation,"International Funding for curatorial research travels for curators, directors of art institutions, art critics, and other art professionals.",Visual arts,funding,Denmark,,"Grants of up to DKK 15,000 per person for travel and accommodation.",,,en,Curatorial Research Programme,"Curators, directors of exhibition venues, art critics and art mediators working with contemporary art. Danish art institutions or other Danish art professionals can apply on behalf of one or more foreign curators, provided that the Danish actor undertakes programming and hosting the foreign curator's visit to Denmark. Applicants with Danish CVR/CPR/ NemKonto must apply via the Danish version of this pool The programme is primarily aimed at applicants who already have contacts on the Danish art scene or candidates who wish to develop a project involving specific Danish artists or institutions. Applicants must be able to organize meetings and studio visits on their own.",Curatorial Research Programme,"Curators, directors of exhibition venues, art critics and art mediators working with contemporary art. Danish art institutions or other Danish art professionals can apply on behalf of one or more foreign curators, provided that the Danish actor undertakes programming and hosting the foreign curator's visit to Denmark. Applicants with Danish CVR/CPR/ NemKonto must apply via the Danish version of this pool The programme is primarily aimed at applicants who already have contacts on the Danish art scene or candidates who wish to develop a project involving specific Danish artists or institutions. Applicants must be able to organize meetings and studio visits on their own.","24.09.2026, 2:00 PM",2026-09-24,2026-09-23 12:37:24.990730+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_823c0bbbc582,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/performing-arts-international-activities,https://portal.slks.dk//TAS_Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=2f02cef278c24c4b80a20035ff8119a1,Danish Arts Foundation,"International Smaller theatres, performing arts groups, independent performing artists and operators organising or working with performing arts activities can apply for grants of max. DKK 100,000 for international performing arts activities.",Performing arts,grants,Denmark,,"grants of max. DKK 100,000",,,en,Performing arts: International activities,"Smaller theatres, performing arts groups, independent performing artists and operators organising or working with performing arts activities can apply for grants of max. DKK 100,000 for international performing arts activities.

Who may apply? Smaller theatres, performing arts groups, independent performing artists and operators organising or working with performing arts activities.

Who may not apply? Support cannot be granted for projects, which are carried out exclusively by the large institutional theatres. By large institutional theatres we mean The Royal Danish Theatre, the Danish regional theatres, the Jutland Opera, and the theatres in the Copenhagen theatre association may not apply. You cannot receive funding for the following purposes activities initiated ahead of the deadline educational purposes for individuals",Performing arts: International activities,"Smaller theatres, performing arts groups, independent performing artists and operators organising or working with performing arts activities can apply for grants of max. DKK 100,000 for international performing arts activities.

Who may apply? Smaller theatres, performing arts groups, independent performing artists and operators organising or working with performing arts activities.

Who may not apply? Support cannot be granted for projects, which are carried out exclusively by the large institutional theatres. By large institutional theatres we mean The Royal Danish Theatre, the Danish regional theatres, the Jutland Opera, and the theatres in the Copenhagen theatre association may not apply. You cannot receive funding for the following purposes activities initiated ahead of the deadline educational purposes for individuals","01.10.2026, 2:00 PM",2026-01-10,2026-09-23 12:37:24.994349+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_091f95df035c,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/nordic-translations,https://portal.slks.dk/Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=e6330c53cf004a46b91c8f2972825f37,Danish Arts Foundation,"Funding for Nordic publishers to cover fees for translators, translating a work from Danish into another Nordic language.",Litteratur Internationalt Literature International,funding,Denmark,,Funding for Nordic publishers to cover fees for translators,,,en,Nordic translations,"Who may apply? Nordic publishers wishing to publish a work translated from Danish into another Nordic language. Non-Nordic publishers: please apply to the fund ‘Literary production and translation’. Applications should be made in the Nordic country in which the work was originally published. For the translation of works from Danish, you should therefore submit your application to the Danish Arts Foundation's Committee for Literary Project Funding. Before submitting the application, the applicant must have acquired the copyrights for the literary work and signed a contract with a translator. Projects may not be finished before the expiry of the application deadline. You can apply for: Fiction for adults, children and young adults General cultural literature and non-fiction Essays Comics and graphic novels You cannot receive funding for: translation of works within the areas of research, education, regional and local history, handbooks, hobby books, self-help books, and catalogues translation of your own works and text revision Furthermore, funding is typically not awarded to Danish publishers for publication of Danish works in translation.",Nordic translations,"Who may apply? Nordic publishers wishing to publish a work translated from Danish into another Nordic language. Non-Nordic publishers: please apply to the fund ‘Literary production and translation’. Applications should be made in the Nordic country in which the work was originally published. For the translation of works from Danish, you should therefore submit your application to the Danish Arts Foundation's Committee for Literary Project Funding. Before submitting the application, the applicant must have acquired the copyrights for the literary work and signed a contract with a translator. Projects may not be finished before the expiry of the application deadline. You can apply for: Fiction for adults, children and young adults General cultural literature and non-fiction Essays Comics and graphic novels You cannot receive funding for: translation of works within the areas of research, education, regional and local history, handbooks, hobby books, self-help books, and catalogues translation of your own works and text revision Furthermore, funding is typically not awarded to Danish publishers for publication of Danish works in translation.","12.02.2027, 2:00 PM",2027-12-02,2026-09-23 12:37:24.998213+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_be0b1bc26009,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/literary-production-and-translation,https://portal.slks.dk/Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=6710d33dda9c469aa7c4ad376579223f,Danish Arts Foundation,"Publishing and translation support for literary works (books, e-books, drama, literary podcasts etc.) for adults, children and young adults.",Literature,support,Denmark,,"Publications: DKK 15,000 in contribution towards the total costs of the publication of books and translations up to 100 pages. DKK 30,000 in contribution towards the total costs of the publication of books and translations up to 300 pages. DKK 50,000 in contribution towards the total costs of the publication of books and translations with more than 300 pages. DKK 100,000 in contribution towards the total costs of especially complex and expensive works. Other media: Literary podcasts: DKK 15,000 – at least 90 minutes, DKK 30,000 – at least 180 minutes, DKK 50,000 – at least 300",no fee,,en,Literary production and translation,"Who may apply? Publishing houses and other publishers of Danish literary works in translation, (organisations etc.) Nordic publishers: please apply to the fund ‘Nordiske oversættelser/Nordic translations’ YOU CAN APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Publication of literature in various formats translated from Danish. If you are applying for grants to cover both production and translation costs, you must apply in a single, combined application per work. You can only apply when you have acquired the rights to the work and signed a contract with the translator named in the application. YOU CANNOT APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Individuals cannot apply for support for translation. The support must be applied for by the publishing publisher. Translation of Danish titles to other Nordic languages. Nordic publishers may apply to the Fund for Nordic Translations/ puljen Nordiske Oversættelser for funding to cover fees for translators who translate a work from Danish into another Nordic language Publication of works in which the literature belongs to the realm of research, education, regional and local history, handbooks, self-help and lifestyle books, dictionaries, catalogues, or similar literature. The work must not have been published before the application deadline. Publishers based in Denmark that apply must be able to render probable that the translation will reach its target group through partnerships or a professional distribution network.",Literary production and translation,"Who may apply? Publishing houses and other publishers of Danish literary works in translation, (organisations etc.) Nordic publishers: please apply to the fund ‘Nordiske oversættelser/Nordic translations’ YOU CAN APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Publication of literature in various formats translated from Danish. If you are applying for grants to cover both production and translation costs, you must apply in a single, combined application per work. You can only apply when you have acquired the rights to the work and signed a contract with the translator named in the application. YOU CANNOT APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Individuals cannot apply for support for translation. The support must be applied for by the publishing publisher. Translation of Danish titles to other Nordic languages. Nordic publishers may apply to the Fund for Nordic Translations/ puljen Nordiske Oversættelser for funding to cover fees for translators who translate a work from Danish into another Nordic language Publication of works in which the literature belongs to the realm of research, education, regional and local history, handbooks, self-help and lifestyle books, dictionaries, catalogues, or similar literature. The work must not have been published before the application deadline. Publishers based in Denmark that apply must be able to render probable that the translation will reach its target group through partnerships or a professional distribution network.","12.02.2027, 2:00 PM",2027-12-02,2026-09-23 12:37:25.001907+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_92d5217dc912,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/sample-translations-from-danish,https://portal.slks.dk/Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=bf0a14e4c53a42ae856ca862b96a669e,Danish Arts Foundation,"Grants for sample translations from Danish of works for adults, children and young adults.",Litteratur Internationalt International Literature,Grants,Denmark,,"A fixed grant of DKK 8,000 is awarded for a 40-page sample translation when the original work is 100 pages or longer. A fixed grant of DKK 3,000 is awarded for sample translations of illustrated literature or when the original work is fewer than 100 pages.",,,en,Sample translations from Danish,"Who may apply? Danish and foreign publishers and agencies. Note: In order to ensure the spreading of art support, you may apply for support for a total of four sample translations. YOU CAN APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Sample translation of a Danish work into a foreign language. YOU CANNOT APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Sample translations of works that the committee assesses belong to the realm of research, education, regional and local history, handbooks, self-help and lifestyle books, dictionaries, catalogues, or similar literature. Sample translations of your own works or text revisions. Projects that were carried out and finished before the expiry of the application deadline.",Sample translations from Danish,"Who may apply? Danish and foreign publishers and agencies. Note: In order to ensure the spreading of art support, you may apply for support for a total of four sample translations. YOU CAN APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Sample translation of a Danish work into a foreign language. YOU CANNOT APPLY FOR GRANTS FOR: Sample translations of works that the committee assesses belong to the realm of research, education, regional and local history, handbooks, self-help and lifestyle books, dictionaries, catalogues, or similar literature. Sample translations of your own works or text revisions. Projects that were carried out and finished before the expiry of the application deadline.","12.02.2027, 2:00 PM",2027-12-02,2026-09-23 12:37:25.005467+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_028cc37c2d3b,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/literary-events-and-projects,https://portal.slks.dk/Dashboard/application/CreateApplication?poolId=78e6b196a2b54016bb4b860d421031db,Danish Arts Foundation,"Support for literary events and projects that focus on Danish literature and authors, as well as mentor support and network support for translators.",Litteratur Internationalt International Literature,Support,Denmark,,"mentor support for translators (a fixed amount of DKK 6,000)",,,en,Literary events and projects,"Organisers of literary events, initiatives and literature presentation projects for children, young adults and adults. The project must be based on Danish literature. Translators and publishers may apply for mentor support for translators, and translators may apply for network support.

The authors, illustrators and translators involved must have published at least one work in Danish. Events with audiences must be available to the public and they must be clearly announced. With regard to applications for mentor support, the translator or publisher may apply for a fixed amount of DKK 6,000 for the course of a concrete translation project. With regard to applications for network support, the committee supports activities in local networks of translators who translate from Danish.",Literary events and projects,"Organisers of literary events, initiatives and literature presentation projects for children, young adults and adults. The project must be based on Danish literature. Translators and publishers may apply for mentor support for translators, and translators may apply for network support.

The authors, illustrators and translators involved must have published at least one work in Danish. Events with audiences must be available to the public and they must be clearly announced. With regard to applications for mentor support, the translator or publisher may apply for a fixed amount of DKK 6,000 for the course of a concrete translation project. With regard to applications for network support, the committee supports activities in local networks of translators who translate from Danish.","12.02.2027, 2:00 PM",2027-12-02,2026-09-23 12:37:25.008677+00:00
kunst_dk_denmark_64e7cbaea368,kunst_dk_denmark,https://www.kunst.dk/english/funding-programmes/craft-and-design-projects-in-denmark-and-abroad,https://portal.slks.dk/Dashboard/Login/?returnUrl=/Dashboard/,Danish Arts Foundation,Funding for projects for and with Danish craft and design in Denmark and abroad.,Crafts & Design,Funding,Denmark,,,,,en,Craft and design projects in Denmark and abroad,"The Committee for Craft and Design Project Funding funds artists, designers, curators, authors, promoters, museums, galleries and others with an interest in developing and promoting craft and design in Denmark and Danish craft and design abroad in the form of projects. You can read more about how the committee defines a project under the ""What is the purpose of the programme"" section of this page. Examples of projects that the committee may fund include: Exhibitions and dissemination projects as well as exhibition series and annual programmes that involve works by contemporary artists and designers in Denmark and/or abroad. Residencies and exchange/work stays Production of works Projects that show aesthetic potential and a thorough understanding of a craft, materials and sensuousness Projects that are centered on concrete design solutions to specific problems or projects that are more immaterial or critical in nature. Presentations and all types of dissemination (verbal, written, visual, digital and printed) of the works of contemporary Danish artists and designers to a relevant audience, this includes travel funding and residencies in connection with specific exhibitions and tasks Funding for establishing a business and international cooperation on the production of new types of Danish craft and design products that contribute to demonstrating the special identity and profile of the craft or design Editorial content production for different media: reviews, articles, dissemination of academic research projects etc. Find out more about how to apply if your project combines different art forms. You cannot receive funding for: Activities completed before the application deadline Courses of study/training courses Projects that the committee have previously supported Capital investments and operating expenses Expenses from previous calendar years. That is, only expenses from either the same or upcoming calendar year can be entered into the budget",Craft and design projects in Denmark and abroad,"The Committee for Craft and Design Project Funding funds artists, designers, curators, authors, promoters, museums, galleries and others with an interest in developing and promoting craft and design in Denmark and Danish craft and design abroad in the form of projects. You can read more about how the committee defines a project under the ""What is the purpose of the programme"" section of this page. Examples of projects that the committee may fund include: Exhibitions and dissemination projects as well as exhibition series and annual programmes that involve works by contemporary artists and designers in Denmark and/or abroad. Residencies and exchange/work stays Production of works Projects that show aesthetic potential and a thorough understanding of a craft, materials and sensuousness Projects that are centered on concrete design solutions to specific problems or projects that are more immaterial or critical in nature. Presentations and all types of dissemination (verbal, written, visual, digital and printed) of the works of contemporary Danish artists and designers to a relevant audience, this includes travel funding and residencies in connection with specific exhibitions and tasks Funding for establishing a business and international cooperation on the production of new types of Danish craft and design products that contribute to demonstrating the special identity and profile of the craft or design Editorial content production for different media: reviews, articles, dissemination of academic research projects etc. Find out more about how to apply if your project combines different art forms. You cannot receive funding for: Activities completed before the application deadline Courses of study/training courses Projects that the committee have previously supported Capital investments and operating expenses Expenses from previous calendar years. That is, only expenses from either the same or upcoming calendar year can be entered into the budget","01.03.2027, 2:00 PM",2027-01-03,2026-09-23 12:37:25.012351+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_1fb6db149626,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/21st-bucharest-international-jazz-competition-2027/,,jmEvents,Open for: instrumentalists and vocalists of all nationalities,jazz,competition,Romania,Bucharest,The total amount of the prizes is 10.000 Euro: cash and concerts engagements. Grand Prize Winner 1.500 Euro Best Band 500 Euro Best Vocalist 500 Euro Best Jam Session 250 Euro 2 – 3 concerts engagements for one or two finalist bands,The registration fee for one application / group is 140 Euro,,en,21st Bucharest International Jazz Competition 2027,"Open for: instrumentalists and vocalists of all nationalities NEW! Age limit: up to 45 years old ( born after the 1st of July 1982 ). The leader can be older than 45. Bands may have up to 6 performing musicians and they may include: instrumentalists and vocalists instrumentalists vocalists Individual musicians can apply for the Jam Session section. Registration in the competition will be made based on digital documents: Application form – Annex A ( for band ), Annex B ( for each member ), Annex C audio recordings for the competition – mp3 / mp4 format two different group photos, color, landscape format, min 1MB copy of the bank confirmation for the payment of the registration fee short presentation of the group – max. 10 lines, word document copy of passport |identity card for EU citizens, for each group’s member technical rider All digital documents will be sent using https://www.transfernow.net/ as follows: make a folder and name it as your band copy all digital documents in the folder archive / compress the folder ( .zip ) send the folder by https://www.transfernow.net/ to email office@jmevents.ro and jmevents.ro@gmail.com please mention: “Application – band’s name”",21st Bucharest International Jazz Competition 2027,"Open for: instrumentalists and vocalists of all nationalities NEW! Age limit: up to 45 years old ( born after the 1st of July 1982 ). The leader can be older than 45. Bands may have up to 6 performing musicians and they may include: instrumentalists and vocalists instrumentalists vocalists Individual musicians can apply for the Jam Session section. Registration in the competition will be made based on digital documents: Application form – Annex A ( for band ), Annex B ( for each member ), Annex C audio recordings for the competition – mp3 / mp4 format two different group photos, color, landscape format, min 1MB copy of the bank confirmation for the payment of the registration fee short presentation of the group – max. 10 lines, word document copy of passport |identity card for EU citizens, for each group’s member technical rider All digital documents will be sent using https://www.transfernow.net/ as follows: make a folder and name it as your band copy all digital documents in the folder archive / compress the folder ( .zip ) send the folder by https://www.transfernow.net/ to email office@jmevents.ro and jmevents.ro@gmail.com please mention: “Application – band’s name”",01 Mar 2027,2027-03-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.015247+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_a923281df709,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/kooperativa-x-fai-mobility-programme-immerse-yourself-in-the-southeastern-european-arts-sector/,https://www.are.na/login?redirectTo=%2Fward-bosmans%2Fflanders-see-hangout%2Finvite%2Fl05x6flkHjoMWA8_8hRjuw,"Flanders Arts Institute, Kooperativa","From June 2026 to September 2027, Flanders Arts Institute will support artists and arts professionals who wish to immerse themselves in the South-Eastern European arts sector . Together with Kooperativa we’re starting this mobility programme, aiming to deepen our understanding of each other’s sector and practices, to build bridges of exchange and solidarity, and to share the gained experiences with our own arts sectors.","visual arts, performing arts, music and sound",mobility programme,Flanders,,The mobility funding covers: travel; accommodation; per diems; a support of up to 300 euros for the host to cover any costs they might incur. The budgets will be calculated according to Erasmus+ formulas.,,,en,Kooperativa x FAI mobility programme: Immerse yourself in the South-Eastern European arts sector,"This call is for Flemish artists and arts professionals in the fields of visual arts, performing arts, music and sound.",Kooperativa x FAI mobility programme: Immerse yourself in the South-Eastern European arts sector,"This call is for Flemish artists and arts professionals in the fields of visual arts, performing arts, music and sound.",1 March 2027,2027-03-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.018597+00:00
