kunsten_be_flanders_24c1762e9c89,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/design-the-worlds-first-permanent-public-memorial-dedicated-to-the-victims-of-the-climate-crisis/,https://www.climatejusticeforrosa.org/open-call,"Climate Justice for Rosa, Greenpeace, Amnesty International, Oxfam and the Climate Coalition","We are calling upon artists, architects, designers, scenographers, and creative collectives to contribute to the creation of a public memorial dedicated to the victims of the global climate crisis.","artists, architects, designers, scenographers, and creative collectives",Commission,Belgium,Brussels,"The estimated production budget we can currently foresee is around €25,000 . At this stage, approximately €20,000 has already been secured.",,,en,Design the World’s First Permanent Public Memorial Dedicated to the Victims of the Climate Crisis,"We are currently looking for expressions of interest . At this preliminary stage, we require answers to the following questions: Are you interested in contributing to this project? Are you available to actively engage in the process over the coming weeks? Can you commit to delivering a first concept proposal by July 1st, 2026 ? Your first conceptual proposal may include: Sketches, conceptual notes, or baseline visualizations.",Design the World’s First Permanent Public Memorial Dedicated to the Victims of the Climate Crisis,"We are currently looking for expressions of interest . At this preliminary stage, we require answers to the following questions: Are you interested in contributing to this project? Are you available to actively engage in the process over the coming weeks? Can you commit to delivering a first concept proposal by July 1st, 2026 ? Your first conceptual proposal may include: Sketches, conceptual notes, or baseline visualizations.",15 Jun 2026,2026-06-15,2026-09-23 12:37:25.180501+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_73af767aad70,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/a-work-for-kanal-before-kanal-opens/,https://forms.gle/kBDDPC2bH5g9zB6z9,KANAL–Centre Pompidou,"In September 2026, before its public opening, KANAL–Centre Pompidou hosts Zero Horizon , a new iteration of Miniature by Alexander Schellow and David Weber-Krebs. The project takes place in a museum building in transition, between completion and public activation. We are looking for twelve participants for a process-based performative work combining workshops, rehearsals, and performative encounters.",performance,Open call,Belgium,Brussels,Participants will receive a fee based on an estimated average rate of €27 per hour of active performance time. Catering will be provided during workshop and rehearsal days.,,,en,A work for KANAL before KANAL opens,No prior professional experience in performance is required. Participants contribute to situated individual and speculative narratives embedded in the architectural and institutional context. A connection to the local context and openness to collaborative work are essential.,A work for KANAL before KANAL opens,No prior professional experience in performance is required. Participants contribute to situated individual and speculative narratives embedded in the architectural and institutional context. A connection to the local context and openness to collaborative work are essential.,14 Jun 2026,2026-06-14,2026-09-23 12:37:25.186918+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_9b6a847d32f1,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/pitch-your-idea-during-the-zminaresilience-x-benelux-networking-session/,https://platform.izolyatsia.org/en/events/zmina-benelux-2026/,"Creative Europe Desks of Flanders, Wallonia-Brussels, Luxembourg, and the Netherlands","On 24 June 2026, ZMINA:Resilience team, together with the Creative Europe Desks of Flanders, Wallonia-Brussels, Luxembourg, and the Netherlands, invites cultural and creative organisations from the Benelux region to a dedicated networking session. This event is designed for those looking to connect with Ukrainian cultural organisations and explore collaboration opportunities within the framework of Creative Europe’s special calls supporting Ukraine . Whether you have a project concept ready or are simply looking to discover what Ukrainian organisations are working on — this session offers a structured and results-oriented space to find future partners.",cultural and creative sectors,networking session,Benelux region,,"This call will allow organizations to apply for up to €25,000 to create new cultural productions between organizations from Ukraine and other Creative Europe countries (see past call for reference). Showcasing rolling call: Starting in June 2026, new calls for showcasing of existing artistic work will open every two months (following the Culture Moves Europe model) with up to €50,000 co-financing to present existing works and practices for new audiences.",,,en,Pitch your idea during the ZMINA:Resilience × Benelux Networking Session,"Organizational Focus: Grants are available to legal entities/organizations. Open Sectoral Approach: No strict sectoral restrictions; participation is open to all cultural and creative sectors with a focus on participatory and socially-engaged work. Limitation is the Audiovisual sector (MEDIA). Benelux Interest: Specifically tailored for organizations from Flanders, Luxembourg, the Netherlands, and Wallonia looking for high-impact international cooperation with Ukraine.",Pitch your idea during the ZMINA:Resilience × Benelux Networking Session,"Organizational Focus: Grants are available to legal entities/organizations. Open Sectoral Approach: No strict sectoral restrictions; participation is open to all cultural and creative sectors with a focus on participatory and socially-engaged work. Limitation is the Audiovisual sector (MEDIA). Benelux Interest: Specifically tailored for organizations from Flanders, Luxembourg, the Netherlands, and Wallonia looking for high-impact international cooperation with Ukraine.",14 Jun 2026,2026-06-14,2026-09-23 12:37:25.189822+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_ad6b7bb11552,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-apprentice-master-season-2026-2027/,https://kunstpodium-t.com/tips/open-call-apprentice-master-season-2026-2-2,Kunstpodium T,"Are you ready to develop your practice in our experimental project space? This within a vibrant network of fellow starting ánd renowned artists? Then mark june 5th 23:00 in your calendar, the deadline for our Apprentice Master program.",artists,Open call,Belgium,Tilburg,Participation is compensated with a decent exhibition fee.,,recently graduated artists,en,Open call Apprentice/Master season 2026 – 2027,"This season we’ll select 28 recently graduated artists, they will be divided into 7 different groups. *It is possible to apply as an autodidact. Please send an e-mail to contact@kunstpodium-t.com . We will determine your eligibility for our program on a case-by-case basis.",Open call Apprentice/Master season 2026 – 2027,"This season we’ll select 28 recently graduated artists, they will be divided into 7 different groups. *It is possible to apply as an autodidact. Please send an e-mail to contact@kunstpodium-t.com . We will determine your eligibility for our program on a case-by-case basis.",05 Jun 2026,2026-06-05,2026-09-23 12:37:25.192574+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_4d016b2d08b2,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-perfomers-kostuum-en-modeontwerpers/,,kunsten.be,"Rumour has it that, after an extremely wonderful, but very much kept under the radar first edition, a second ‘Dress-up-tea-Party’ is being organised. This time, with some budget, and the courage to be more of a public event. Performers are invited to come and spill some tea, serve tea and infuse the tea room with their character.",performers; costume- & fashion designers,Open Call,Belgium,Brussels,Artist honorarium fee €100,,,en,Open Call for performers and costume- & fashion designers,"We are inviting anyone to send us a proposal to create a performance, character or small happening around the (social) aspects of drinking tea (ceremonial, historical, colonial, its gossipy aspect etc) to be presented during our Dress-up-tea-Party.

For the ‘Dress-up’ part of our party, we welcome fashion- & costume designers to send a proposal of a selection of pieces/ costumes (from their oeuvre) to be used during the Dress-Up-Tea-Party. Your pieces will be actively worn by visitors/participants and will be handled with care.",Open Call for performers and costume- & fashion designers,"We are inviting anyone to send us a proposal to create a performance, character or small happening around the (social) aspects of drinking tea (ceremonial, historical, colonial, its gossipy aspect etc) to be presented during our Dress-up-tea-Party.

For the ‘Dress-up’ part of our party, we welcome fashion- & costume designers to send a proposal of a selection of pieces/ costumes (from their oeuvre) to be used during the Dress-Up-Tea-Party. Your pieces will be actively worn by visitors/participants and will be handled with care.",01 Jun 2026,2026-06-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.196257+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_dbee5b009884,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-summerlab-met-dan-daw-bij-p-a-r-t-s/,,Platform K,"Ben je een ervaren performer met of zonder beperking en wil je je verdiepen in inclusieve danspraktijken met een sterke focus op reflectie? Platform K werd gevraagd om tijdens de jaarlijkse SummerSchool van P.A.R.T.S. een SummerLab te cureren rond inclusieve danspraktijk. Dit jaar nodigen we choreografen Dan Daw (VK/Australië) en Sarah Blanc (VK/Ierland) uit om deze week te begeleiden, die plaatsvindt van 13 tot 17 juli 2026 . Het SummerLab biedt de kans om kennis te maken met de werkwijze van Dan Daw Creative Projects (DDCP). Samen met choreografen Dan Daw (VK/Australië) en Sarah Blanc (VK/Ierland) ontwikkelen we choreografisch materiaal vertrekkend vanuit thema’s als individuele en collectieve veerkracht – ontleend aan DDCP’s nieuwste werk EXXY . Dit doen we door te improviseren, teksten te schrijven en gesprekken te voeren.",dans / performancekunst,Workshop,Belgium,Brussels,We werken met een pay what you can -systeem. De bijdrage voor de volledige week bedraagt: €250 (richtprijs) / €200 (verminderd tarief).,We werken met een pay what you can -systeem. De bijdrage voor de volledige week bedraagt: €250 (richtprijs) / €200 (verminderd tarief).,ervaren performer,en,Open call: SummerLab met Dan Daw bij P.A.R.T.S.,"Ben je een ervaren performer met of zonder beperking en wil je je verdiepen in inclusieve danspraktijken met een sterke focus op reflectie?

