kunsten_be_flanders_66619beb67ef,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/helsinki-international-curatorial-programme-hicp/,,Frame Contemporary Art Finland and HIAP,We’re welcoming applications from international curators for a 1-month residency at HIAP Suomenlinna.,curators,Residency,,Helsinki,"The residency includes a €1200 working grant, a combined living and working space at HIAP Suomenlinna, and a travel allowance (with slow travel encouraged).",,2–3+ years professional curatorial experience,en,Helsinki International Curatorial Programme (HICP),Who can apply: Curators based outside Finland with 2–3+ years professional curatorial experience (institutional or independent).,Helsinki International Curatorial Programme (HICP),Who can apply: Curators based outside Finland with 2–3+ years professional curatorial experience (institutional or independent).,"Mon 23 Feb 2026, 15:00 (GMT+2)",2026-02-23,2026-09-23 12:37:25.311738+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_7b3d4f68b4d8,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/auditions-conversations-new-xrperformance-by-paul-boereboom-leon-rogissart/,,Paul Boereboom and Leon Rogissart,"Conversations is a new music theatre production by Paul Boereboom and Leon Rogissart. An immersive music theatre ritual for an intimate audience of 80 participants. In a shared space, performers and audience move together through a collective experience of music, reflection, and encounter. The performance is participatory and interactive. As a performer, you engage directly with the audience: you are not playing a character, but performing as yourself. Presence, attentiveness, and openness towards the participants are central to the work. The project explores themes of inner dialogue, presence, and collective ritual, and uses technology as a supportive dramaturgical layer rather than a dominant element.",classical vocal performers,Audition,null,Rotterdam,"7 paid rehearsal days (dates to be confirmed, scheduled in April-May) and 2 paid performance days on the 24th and the 25th of May.",,,en,Auditions Conversations – New XRPerformance by Paul Boereboom & Leon Rogissart,"We are looking for vocal performers who: _have a classical alt / baritone/tenor vocal range _are comfortable with live performance and embodied presence _enjoy participatory interaction with an audience _have affinity with music theatre, contemporary music, and/or ritual practices _enjoy collaborative, research-driven creation processes",Auditions Conversations – New XRPerformance by Paul Boereboom & Leon Rogissart,"We are looking for vocal performers who: _have a classical alt / baritone/tenor vocal range _are comfortable with live performance and embodied presence _enjoy participatory interaction with an audience _have affinity with music theatre, contemporary music, and/or ritual practices _enjoy collaborative, research-driven creation processes",23 Feb 2026,2026-02-23,2026-09-23 12:37:25.315538+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_399ae984ab54,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/printmaking-residency-milaan/,http://www.gate44.eu/open-call/,Gate44,"Gate 44 is pleased to announce an international Open Call for artists and creatives, among which one will be awarded a production based residency in the field of printmaking in our Milan workshop.",printmaking,Residency,Italy,Milan,"2 weeks funded production residency at our Milan facility within the period between April 2026 and April 2027 (specific dates to be determined in collaboration with the selected participant). Technical assistance. A dedicated and skilled technical team providing guidance and hands-on support for the production of one or more editions. A budget of 1000 € spendable in materials. Private on-site apartment equipped with a kitchen, bathroom, and courtyard, near to the print studio, for the full duration of the residency. 24/7 access to a state-of-the-art production space equipped for: relief printing, intaglio techniques, photo-lithography, photo-polymer, screen printing, letterpress, digital fine art. Detailed list of equipments. Basic print-shop materials and tools included (cleaning agents, solvents, rags, spatulas, squeegees, rollers etc.) Social media coverage and a feature on Gate44’s website.",€30,,en,Printmaking residency (Milaan),"Artists whose practice already includes printmaking to some extent. Artists who have a minimum base knowledge and understanding of one or more print techniques (even though professional technical assistance will be provided). Artists who are eager to expand their technical tool-kit and expressive potential. Artists who embrace experimentation, interdisciplinary approaches, and the blending of multiple printmaking methods.

Must be able to travel to Milan for the scheduled residency, and be able to use the provided materials and equipment. Uphold a professional work ethic and conduct throughout the residency. Work must fit within a maximum paper size of 50 × 70 cm (no minimum size). A minimum production of 10 finished prints is required. Create a minimum of one printed edition or multiple unique pieces. Agree to provide n. 3 (three) copies of each edition printed to Gate44’s archives.",Printmaking residency (Milaan),"Artists whose practice already includes printmaking to some extent. Artists who have a minimum base knowledge and understanding of one or more print techniques (even though professional technical assistance will be provided). Artists who are eager to expand their technical tool-kit and expressive potential. Artists who embrace experimentation, interdisciplinary approaches, and the blending of multiple printmaking methods.

Must be able to travel to Milan for the scheduled residency, and be able to use the provided materials and equipment. Uphold a professional work ethic and conduct throughout the residency. Work must fit within a maximum paper size of 50 × 70 cm (no minimum size). A minimum production of 10 finished prints is required. Create a minimum of one printed edition or multiple unique pieces. Agree to provide n. 3 (three) copies of each edition printed to Gate44’s archives.",22 February 2026,2026-02-22,2026-09-23 12:37:25.318979+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_3239893e64df,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-curatorial-fellow-public-outreach-community-engagement/,,Kunsthal Mechelen and the Curatorial Studies programme at KASK & Conservatorium,"Kunsthal Mechelen —an open house for contemporary art in Mechelen—and the Curatorial Studies programme at KASK & Conservatorium are partnering for the third time to offer young curators a paid, institution-based opportunity, this year within the framework of Contour Biennale .",Curatorial Studies,Open call,Belgium,Mechelen,"We offer a BIS/CIP internship of 6 months (Beroepsinlevingsovereenkomst), to be spread between the beginning of March and end of October. Remuneration: amount to be determined.",null,young curators,en,Open Call: Curatorial Fellow – Public Outreach & Community Engagement,"We are looking for someone who: Has a background in curatorial practice, museum studies, or arts education. Can combine conceptual thinking with practical programme design. Is enthusiastic about community engagement and building volunteer networks. Enjoys experimenting with formats for children, families, and multigenerational audiences. Values collaboration and can work across departments to integrate public-facing activities into the curatorial vision. Can support the team with research of accessibility / public outreach related grants. Has strong communicative and writing skills in English and Dutch.",Open Call: Curatorial Fellow – Public Outreach & Community Engagement,"We are looking for someone who: Has a background in curatorial practice, museum studies, or arts education. Can combine conceptual thinking with practical programme design. Is enthusiastic about community engagement and building volunteer networks. Enjoys experimenting with formats for children, families, and multigenerational audiences. Values collaboration and can work across departments to integrate public-facing activities into the curatorial vision. Can support the team with research of accessibility / public outreach related grants. Has strong communicative and writing skills in English and Dutch.",22 Feb 2026,2026-02-22,2026-09-23 12:37:25.322356+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_fbadd44e7fb1,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/call-for-submissions-file-electronic-language-international-festival/,https://file.org.br/highlight/file-2026-inscricoes-abertas-para-festival-de-arte-e-tecnologia/,FILE – International Electronic Language Festival,"FILE – Electronic Language International Festival is now accepting project submissions and invites artists, researchers, creators, and developers to participate in its next edition.",art and technology,call for submissions,Brazil,São Paulo,,,,en,Call for submissions: FILE – Electronic Language International Festival,"FILE invites Brazilian and international artists , as well as researchers, educators, and creators , to submit original artistic works and educational proposals — lectures, workshops, and training activities — focused on contemporary technological poetics.",Call for submissions: FILE – Electronic Language International Festival,"FILE invites Brazilian and international artists , as well as researchers, educators, and creators , to submit original artistic works and educational proposals — lectures, workshops, and training activities — focused on contemporary technological poetics.",19 Feb 2026,2026-02-19,2026-09-23 12:37:25.325781+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_d04919f3f6f8,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-code-2026-reclaiming-digital-agency/,https://tally.so/r/9q90a4,IMPAKT [Centre for Media Culture],"CODE 2026 is a five-month co-creation trajectory running from April to July 2026. Participants will work in interdisciplinary groups, guided by mentors, through a series of physical and remote meetings. The programme consists of five on-site appointments, two remote working moments with mentors, and a final three-day hackathon, which will take place at the end of the co-creation process.","artists, designer, researcher, software designer or developer",open call,the Netherlands and Belgium,Utrecht,,,,en,Open call: CODE 2026 – Reclaiming Digital Agency,"Are you an artist, designer, researcher, software designer or developer? Working in marketing, law, technology, policymaking, politics? Interested in human rights and equality? Are you open to working on collaborative projects that can speak to the imagination of a wider audience and inspire them to think about their digital agency? If you answered yes to any of these questions, or if you’re simply concerned about our digital rights and the lack of agency across the online platforms we use, then IMPAKT is looking for you! ... we invite creatives, professional and non-professional artists, and concerned citizens of the Netherlands and Belgium to embark on a journey of critical discourse and collaborative creation regarding digital rights.",Open call: CODE 2026 – Reclaiming Digital Agency,"Are you an artist, designer, researcher, software designer or developer? Working in marketing, law, technology, policymaking, politics? Interested in human rights and equality? Are you open to working on collaborative projects that can speak to the imagination of a wider audience and inspire them to think about their digital agency? If you answered yes to any of these questions, or if you’re simply concerned about our digital rights and the lack of agency across the online platforms we use, then IMPAKT is looking for you! ... we invite creatives, professional and non-professional artists, and concerned citizens of the Netherlands and Belgium to embark on a journey of critical discourse and collaborative creation regarding digital rights.",15 Feb 2026 (before 23:59 CET),2027-02-15,2026-09-23 12:37:25.355779+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_465e8f51003f,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-bba-one-shot-award-winter-2026/,https://bba-prizes.com/one-shot-award,BBA Gallery,Your Story. Your Medium. The BBA One Shot Award Winter 2026 invites photographers from around the world to share their vision in a single image. This international open call is a celebration of photography and image-making in all its forms – from analogue film to DSLR to smartphone. The tool you use doesn’t matter. What matters is the spark of a story captured in one decisive moment.,photography and image-making,award,Germany,Berlin,,,,en,Open call: BBA One Shot Award Winter 2026,"Open to everyone aged 18+, the award welcomes multiple entries and embraces all lens-based mediums.",Open call: BBA One Shot Award Winter 2026,"Open to everyone aged 18+, the award welcomes multiple entries and embraces all lens-based mediums.","Monday, 26 January 2026",2026-01-26,2026-09-23 12:37:25.359737+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_ab2801ef4c6f,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-word-artist-in-residence-bij-muziekhuis-rataplan-2026/,https://www.cognitoforms.com/Rataplan1/ArtistInResidenceRataplanOpenCall2026,Rataplan,"Rataplan is a music venue, a home for jazz, with a stage, a shared breeding ground and a broad, intergenerational community. Each season, they offer four musical residencies that focus on development, experimentation, exchange and presentation. Will you be the new Artist in Residence in 2026/27?",musical,Residency,,,five days of financial compensation and tailored support,,"Up-and-coming, musical, professional talent with a unique approach to jazz. Also mid-career artists",en,Become Artist in Residence at music venue Rataplan,"Up-and-coming, musical, professional talent with a unique approach to jazz. Also mid-career artists who collaborate across generations on a surprising and adventurous project that enriches the jazz scene. Musicians or collectives with projects that meet the following criteria: Your practice is based on jazz and can be enhanced by other art forms. These can be other music genres, encounters with performance (theatre, slam poetry, dance, etc.), visual/audiovisual art. Proposals aimed at a young audience are also eligible. You are an emerging, professional and adventurous musician with a determined outlook on the future. Or you have been active for some time and are working on an innovative project. You pay attention to a variety of sounds and representation in your band. The residency focuses on artistic development. It is not part of an academic research study, the completion of an album or rehearsals for a release. You will be part of the Rataplan breeding ground: you will engage in dialogue with the other residents, share expertise and be present during other performances. You are interested and open to collaboration with Rataplan. This is an additional commitment that you take on as an artist in residence. You have an affinity with jazz in connection with the metropolitan context. Your music reflects the urban soundscape.",Become Artist in Residence at music venue Rataplan,"Up-and-coming, musical, professional talent with a unique approach to jazz. Also mid-career artists who collaborate across generations on a surprising and adventurous project that enriches the jazz scene. Musicians or collectives with projects that meet the following criteria: Your practice is based on jazz and can be enhanced by other art forms. These can be other music genres, encounters with performance (theatre, slam poetry, dance, etc.), visual/audiovisual art. Proposals aimed at a young audience are also eligible. You are an emerging, professional and adventurous musician with a determined outlook on the future. Or you have been active for some time and are working on an innovative project. You pay attention to a variety of sounds and representation in your band. The residency focuses on artistic development. It is not part of an academic research study, the completion of an album or rehearsals for a release. You will be part of the Rataplan breeding ground: you will engage in dialogue with the other residents, share expertise and be present during other performances. You are interested and open to collaboration with Rataplan. This is an additional commitment that you take on as an artist in residence. You have an affinity with jazz in connection with the metropolitan context. Your music reflects the urban soundscape.",18 January 2026,2026-01-18,2026-09-23 12:37:25.362659+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_d3e08cdf7f83,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-bosacademie/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfb0m1HNOgYbbnOPtUSi0ZbJGfIq5NKnmB59KM9muyr7GFYKQ/viewform,Het Bos,"Bosacademie is a development program for young people in Het Bos. It’s a springboard for your own projects and ideas. Bosacademie can be described as an education, a brainstorming session, a learning path, and a presentation platform for young thinkers and doers, as well as artists and creative entrepreneurs. Bosacademie offers you a wide range of opportunities to explore Het Bos and network with other artists and organizations!",artists and creative entrepreneurs,development program,Belgium,Antwerp,"Working hours and a workspace at Het Bos in April, May, July, August, or September, minimum 5 days and maximum 20 days Possible presentation platform, such as the Vruchtbare Grond festival, which will take place from May 14th to 24th and September 17th to 26th. Het Bos will provide promotion and technical and production support. A small participation fee, via Amplo, of at least €150. Coaching by professionals",no fee stated,young people,en,Open Call Bosacademie,"You are between 18 and 28 years old. You live in Belgium and/or independently reach Het Bos (Ankerrui 5/7, Antwerp) Your project includes a public performance as a closing or interim presentation Your project aligns with Het Bos’s mission. You actively participate in the Boscademie project. We meet an average of 7 times a year. Project proposals are selected based on feasibility, necessity, focus, and relevance, among other factors. We appreciate it if you involve one or more communities in your project.",Open Call Bosacademie,"You are between 18 and 28 years old. You live in Belgium and/or independently reach Het Bos (Ankerrui 5/7, Antwerp) Your project includes a public performance as a closing or interim presentation Your project aligns with Het Bos’s mission. You actively participate in the Boscademie project. We meet an average of 7 times a year. Project proposals are selected based on feasibility, necessity, focus, and relevance, among other factors. We appreciate it if you involve one or more communities in your project.",14 Jan 2026,2026-01-14,2026-09-23 12:37:25.366496+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_eb5a557cfc39,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-bba-artist-prize-2026/,https://bba-prizes.com/artist-prize,BBA,"We invite artists from around the world to apply for the BBA Artist Prize 2026. All mediums and themes are welcome, and the competition is open to anyone 18+, regardless of experience, education, or background.",All mediums and themes,Artist Prize,,BBA Gallery,,,"established artist, an emerging talent, or simply passionate about creating",en,Open Call – BBA Artist Prize 2026,"open to anyone 18+, regardless of experience, education, or background.",Open Call – BBA Artist Prize 2026,"open to anyone 18+, regardless of experience, education, or background.",12 Jan 2026,2026-01-12,2026-09-23 12:37:25.369877+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_857be5e8a36a,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/bicentennial-of-photography-labeling-call-for-projects/,https://www.culture.gouv.fr/en/catalogue-des-demarches-et-subventions/appels-a-projets-candidatures/bicentennial-of-photography-labeling-call-for-projects,Ministère de la culture Française,"Photography was invented nearly two centuries ago. To mark this occasion, the French Ministry of Culture is planning a large, community-wide celebration of the Bicentennial of Photography, showcasing photography in all its forms throughout France from September 2026 to September 2027. All those involved in photography, the arts and culture are invited to join the celebrations by organizing events, exhibitions, meet-ups, hands-on projects, talks, publications and educational workshops to make it a major cultural event.",Photography,Call for Projects,France,,"Official labeling, inclusion on an interactive map and a dedicated website will maximize exposure for the selected events.",,,en,‘Bicentennial of Photography’ Labeling: Call for Projects,The call for projects is open to applicants from France and abroad .,‘Bicentennial of Photography’ Labeling: Call for Projects,The call for projects is open to applicants from France and abroad .,11 Jan 2026,2026-01-11,2026-09-23 12:37:25.373134+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_2ed3f7c14414,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/ga-mee-met-vonk-op-4-daags-netwerkprogramma-in-berlijn/,https://kunstplaatsvonk.be/en/activities/open-call-internationaal-programma-berlijn-2026,Kunstplaats Vonk,"Kunstplaats Vonk is organ­is­ing a four-day net­work­ing pro­gram in Berlin. During this event, from June 7 th to June 12 th 2026 , Vonk will bring 8 emerg­ing visu­al artists from Belgium to Berlin to fur­ther devel­op their pro­fes­sion­al networks.",Visual Artists,networking program,Belgium,Berlin,"A shared hotel room for 5 nights in Berlin (2 people per room, single beds), including breakfast 6 one-on-one meetings with 8 German curators (gallery owners, artistic directors, programmers, etc.) including lunch and dinner on Monday 8 June 2026 3 guided visits at art organisations in Berlin",Pay a contribution of € 363.00 (incl. 21% VAT) to cover part of our costs (A payment plan is possible if needed),emerging,en,Join Vonk on a four-day networking program in Berlin,Visual Artists Active in visual arts or in trans­disciplinary performing arts Demonstrating a high artistic quality With a solid professional career in Belgium You Should Be available on 4 April 2026 for an introductory meeting in Hasselt Be free to travel for the duration of the program: 7 – 12 June 2026 Hold a Belgian nationality or have lived in Belgium for at least 3 years Prepare your own portfolio,Join Vonk on a four-day networking program in Berlin,Visual Artists Active in visual arts or in trans­disciplinary performing arts Demonstrating a high artistic quality With a solid professional career in Belgium You Should Be available on 4 April 2026 for an introductory meeting in Hasselt Be free to travel for the duration of the program: 7 – 12 June 2026 Hold a Belgian nationality or have lived in Belgium for at least 3 years Prepare your own portfolio,09 Jan 2026,2026-01-09,2026-09-23 12:37:25.376237+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_61e96ffd7526,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-masterclass-movement-performativity-togetherness/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScYla2Pon8MPTUPibGpd5cZceiDaw0-BIl3qxqh2KjHOH60yA/viewform,TOGETHERNESS,"TOGETHERNESS is organising a masterclass on dance and movement about security, togetherness and the power of being together, culminating in a public performance.",dance and movement,masterclass,,Ghent,,"A contribution of 100 euros is requested for participation in the project, covering all rehearsals, performances, insurance and other costs for the project",,en,Open call: Masterclass movement & performativity TOGETHERNESS,"TOGETHERNESS is looking for eight dancers/movement artists who are interested in exploring, creating and supporting the project.

What are our requirements for participation?
