kunsten_be_flanders_8e81a92d284b,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/kunstenaar-gezocht-voor-participatief-project-in-sint-agatha-berchem/,https://forms.office.com/Pages/ResponsePage.aspx?id=5VYrkWCavke4UrG501iDNIKO_mxb6O5Mq8Tb_x8Xku5UNkpWMUhFQkUyM1lWN05VT1pBWDFJQk9PVC4u,"Gemeenschapscentrum De Kroon, Archipel19","The socio-cultural centres De Kroon and Archipel19 in Sint-Agatha-Berchem are looking for an artist interested in co-creation, who wants to develop an artistic programme that creates connection in the public space, together with local residents.","image, movement and interaction",Commission,Belgium,Sint-Agatha-Berchem,"There is a total budget of €19,500 for the project. This includes all the costs.",,,en,Artist sought for Participatory Project in Sint-Agatha-Berchem,"The socio-cultural centres De Kroon and Archipel19 in Sint-Agatha-Berchem are looking for an artist interested in co-creation, who wants to develop an artistic programme that creates connection in the public space, together with local residents. Are you someone who knows how to harness the power of imagery and nonverbal communication to bring people closer together? Would you like to work with an intergenerational group of residents around Parc Pirsoul? Then this project is for you.

You will develop an artistic programme with and for the neighbourhood. Together with residents, you will work on creating playful, visual installations in the public space .

As an artist, you will design a co-creative programme: You will organise contact sessions with the neighbourhood in the park or in socio-cultural centre De Kroon/Archipel19 during the period March – June 2026. You will be actively engaged in the neighbourhood and work with residents and local partners . From idea to end result, co-creation is the core focus, with essential input from an intergenerational group of participants . Socio-cultural centre De Kroon and Archipel19 will put together this group of residents for the project. Archipel10 and De Kroon will also support you during the process in further empowering this group of neighbourhood residents. You will focus on language-transcending connection through images and action, not (only) through words. Together, you will develop a visible, tangible and sustainable end result that lasts beyond the project. You will work with the target group towards a powerful artistic end result that is supported by the neighbourhood. Along with the socio-cultural worker at the socio-cultural centre, you will generate involvement on the part of the target group and partners, and act with respect for the participants. You will pay special attention to those whose voice is not always heard and will actively seek out these voices. You will work within the specified budget.

The group will grow through the process: everyone is welcome, with no barriers or exclusivity.",Artist sought for Participatory Project in Sint-Agatha-Berchem,"The socio-cultural centres De Kroon and Archipel19 in Sint-Agatha-Berchem are looking for an artist interested in co-creation, who wants to develop an artistic programme that creates connection in the public space, together with local residents. Are you someone who knows how to harness the power of imagery and nonverbal communication to bring people closer together? Would you like to work with an intergenerational group of residents around Parc Pirsoul? Then this project is for you.

You will develop an artistic programme with and for the neighbourhood. Together with residents, you will work on creating playful, visual installations in the public space .

As an artist, you will design a co-creative programme: You will organise contact sessions with the neighbourhood in the park or in socio-cultural centre De Kroon/Archipel19 during the period March – June 2026. You will be actively engaged in the neighbourhood and work with residents and local partners . From idea to end result, co-creation is the core focus, with essential input from an intergenerational group of participants . Socio-cultural centre De Kroon and Archipel19 will put together this group of residents for the project. Archipel10 and De Kroon will also support you during the process in further empowering this group of neighbourhood residents. You will focus on language-transcending connection through images and action, not (only) through words. Together, you will develop a visible, tangible and sustainable end result that lasts beyond the project. You will work with the target group towards a powerful artistic end result that is supported by the neighbourhood. Along with the socio-cultural worker at the socio-cultural centre, you will generate involvement on the part of the target group and partners, and act with respect for the participants. You will pay special attention to those whose voice is not always heard and will actively seek out these voices. You will work within the specified budget.

The group will grow through the process: everyone is welcome, with no barriers or exclusivity.",18 Dec 2025,2025-12-18,2026-09-23 12:37:25.416539+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_962385d3c6bf,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/farm-studio-india-international-artist-residency-in-rural-rajasthan-2/,https://farmingstudio.wordpress.com/art-residency/,Farm Studio India,"Residency Farm Studio International Artist Residency is located in a rural community in India. Residents stay and create in a quiet art centre and beautiful environment where they can develop their artwork free from accustomed distractions. Here, collaboration and experimentation is encouraged. Relationships form between the artists coming from different countries and varied social, cultural, and artistic backgrounds. Many exciting exchanges and dialogues among artists take place, including scheduled artist talks, presentations, works in progress showings, etc. Farm Studio also promotes and celebrates the local community’s artistic and cultural identity while also introducing art and culture of others’ (Indian and International guests) back to the community. This intercultural exchange broadens everyone’s experiences and fosters art appreciation.",Artists of all disciplines creating in any media,Residency,India,Andore Village,,,,en,Farm Studio India – International Artist Residency in Rural Rajasthan,Artists of all disciplines creating in any media are welcome to apply.,Farm Studio India – International Artist Residency in Rural Rajasthan,Artists of all disciplines creating in any media are welcome to apply.,15 Dec 2025,2025-12-15,2026-09-23 12:37:25.420032+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_63435520343a,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/ga-op-residentie-bij-morpho-in-antwerpen/,https://morphoantwerp.be/en/open-calls/curatorial-residency-goethe-institut-brussel,Goethe-Institut Brüssel and MORPHO,"The Goethe-Institut Brüssel and MORPHO are delighted to inaugurate their collaboration in 2026 with an international curatorial residency. Goethe-Institut Brüssel supports the participation of one curator based in or from Germany going to Antwerp for a three-month residency, in the framework of a thematic programme that explores curating in times of democratic crisis.",curating,residency,Belgium,Antwerp,Goethe-Institut Brüssel supports the participation of one curator based in or from Germany going to Antwerp for a three-month residency,,,en,Open Call – Curatorial Residency Goethe-Institut Brüssel,"This call is open to German curators and curators based in Germany. You have a proven critical practice dedicated to current democratic processes and opening up visions for the future. You want to focus on curatorial research and to present research results during the residency. You want to engage with the Belgian cultural landscape. You are welcome regardless of age, ethnic-cultural background, gender diversity, neurodiversity, and more. We do our best to accommodate everyone’s needs, but the specific architecture of the building (stairs, no lift) means the residency is not suitable for all conditions. There is only room for 1 adult, possibly with a child (Family top-up: 100 € per month). You are welcome to contact us in advance to discuss your personal situation.",Open Call – Curatorial Residency Goethe-Institut Brüssel,"This call is open to German curators and curators based in Germany. You have a proven critical practice dedicated to current democratic processes and opening up visions for the future. You want to focus on curatorial research and to present research results during the residency. You want to engage with the Belgian cultural landscape. You are welcome regardless of age, ethnic-cultural background, gender diversity, neurodiversity, and more. We do our best to accommodate everyone’s needs, but the specific architecture of the building (stairs, no lift) means the residency is not suitable for all conditions. There is only room for 1 adult, possibly with a child (Family top-up: 100 € per month). You are welcome to contact us in advance to discuss your personal situation.",07 Dec 2025,2025-12-07,2026-09-23 12:37:25.425375+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_22da6aff727f,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/ithaka-26-kunstenfestival-voor-jong-talent/,https://www.loko.be/nl/actualiteit/ithaka-2026-open-call-for-artists-2,LOKO Cultuur,"We are looking for young, emerging artists (students, recent graduates, self-taught) from all disciplines who want to experiment within the theme “Human & Animal”. The theme explores the intimate bond with animals, but also broader societal and academic questions around care, systems, and ecology. Ithaka serves as a crucial springboard for emerging talent. We offer selected artists curatorial and production support, a production budget, and the opportunity to show their work to a large and diverse (student) audience.",all disciplines,Call for Artists,Belgium,Leuven,"We offer selected artists curatorial and production support, a production budget, and the opportunity to show their work to a large and diverse (student) audience.",,"young, emerging artists (students, recent graduates, self-taught)",en,Ithaka ’26: arts festival for young talent,"We are looking for young, emerging artists (students, recent graduates, self-taught) from all disciplines who want to experiment within the theme “Human & Animal”.",Ithaka ’26: arts festival for young talent,"We are looking for young, emerging artists (students, recent graduates, self-taught) from all disciplines who want to experiment within the theme “Human & Animal”.",07 Dec 2025,2025-12-07,2026-09-23 12:37:25.429737+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_b25efb4eb1e8,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/kunstenpunt-zoekt-toekomstdenkers-meerstemmigheid/,https://register.kunsten.be/en/meeting-programmes/detail/185/flanders-arts-institute-seeks-multi-voiced-forward-thinkers/about?preview=cadd170d16f1aa877df29b3a38599f2e55f8ad0a,Flanders Arts Institute,"In 2025 Flanders Arts Institute is launching a three-year project on multi-voicedness in the arts. During this period, we will work together with (hands-on) experts and committed artists, citizens and organisations – inside and outside the arts field – to develop tools to achieve a multi-voiced arts field. In 2025, we will identify barriers and opportunities, which we will then translate into concrete tools. In January and February 2026, we will be organising three days – two intensive days in a small group and a public event – to work on concrete ideas for a multi-voiced arts field.",arts,call,Belgium,Malines,"For participants who are not doing this as part of a paid role at an organisation, we provide fair compensation.",,,en,Flanders Arts Institute seeks multi-voiced forward thinkers,"Individuals with expertise and an interest in multi-voicedness and its intersectional approach. Individuals with lived experience in their field of expertise are an advantage. Who are active in the arts (artist, cultural worker, …). Individuals who are available on 19 and 26 January 2026, from 11 am to 4 pm each day. In Malines.",Flanders Arts Institute seeks multi-voiced forward thinkers,"Individuals with expertise and an interest in multi-voicedness and its intersectional approach. Individuals with lived experience in their field of expertise are an advantage. Who are active in the arts (artist, cultural worker, …). Individuals who are available on 19 and 26 January 2026, from 11 am to 4 pm each day. In Malines.",05 Dec 2025,2025-12-05,2026-09-23 12:37:25.433464+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_70e60edf5971,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/oproep-voor-onderzoeksbeurs-voor-curatoren-in-arles/,https://www.rencontres-arles.com/en/bourse-de-recherche-curatoriale-appel-a-candidatures/,The Rencontres d’Arles,The Rencontres d’Arles is delighted to announce the launch of the new edition of the Curatorial Research Fellowship.,exhibition curators,curatorial research fellowship,,Arles,"The maximum € 20,000 grant includes (1) an initial amount of €5,000 in copyright acquired for the winner of the Rencontres d’Arles Curatorial Award ; and (2) a second amount of €15,000 if approval, to produce the project if presented on Les Rencontres d’Arles program.",,,en,Open call for Curatorial Research Fellowship in Arles,"The Rencontres d’Arles €20,000 curatorial research fellowship is open to all exhibition curators.",Open call for Curatorial Research Fellowship in Arles,"The Rencontres d’Arles €20,000 curatorial research fellowship is open to all exhibition curators.",01 Dec 2025,2025-12-01,2026-09-23 12:37:25.436684+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_77942e92b1c5,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-love-among-the-artists-residency-in-marseille/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeU7SWy-9a8OYt9xQvNHk0NnLMkFAy9MZTdsSLQ-3Nf1Oqfww/viewform,Studio Prouvost,"LATA – Love Among The Artists, a project supported by Studio Prouvost, invites you for a self-directed two-week residency in a sunlit apartment by the Mediterranean Sea in Marseille.",artists,Residency,France,Marseille,A fully equipped 45 m² apartment next to Les Catalans beach,,,en,Open Call – “Love Among The Artists” Residency in Marseille,"We are interested in artists that explore transitions from urban to natural, from concrete to cliffside, from the city’s buzz to the sea’s calm",Open Call – “Love Among The Artists” Residency in Marseille,"We are interested in artists that explore transitions from urban to natural, from concrete to cliffside, from the city’s buzz to the sea’s calm","Sunday, 30 November 2025 (midnight).",2025-11-30,2026-09-23 12:37:25.441455+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_df27ab545c60,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-hosting-as-artistic-practice/,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-hosting-as-artistic-practice/,Globe Aroma,"Globe Aroma is looking for a multidisciplinary artist : a poetic thinker with a practical mind and a social tongue, someone who can gently spark everyone’s imagination. From January to June 2026 , we invite one artist to share a unique time and space with our artistic community in the heart of Brussels. We are looking for a person whose artistic practice is centered around hosting and hospitality, someone who builds an open and curious space where creation can appear unexpectedly. During these six months, you will work with people who feel the desire to create, but who are not artists themselves!",multidisciplinary,open call,Belgium,Brussels,6-month employment via Globe Aroma’s payroll (barema PC 329.01),,,en,OPEN CALL – HOSTING AS ARTISTIC PRACTICE,"We are looking for a person whose artistic practice is centered around hosting and hospitality, someone who builds an open and curious space where creation can appear unexpectedly.

We are looking for someone who: works across disciplines (textile, movement, ceramics, poetry, cooking, etc.); blends art, hospitality, care, and community; feels comfortable in multilingual settings; is familiar with migration (by lived experience or affinity); can listen, let go, and stay open to the unexpected; prefers process over product; enjoys collaborating with people with no artistic training but strong imagination.

We especially welcome applications from artists with migration backgrounds, artists of color, queer, neurodiverse, and non-binary artists.",OPEN CALL – HOSTING AS ARTISTIC PRACTICE,"We are looking for a person whose artistic practice is centered around hosting and hospitality, someone who builds an open and curious space where creation can appear unexpectedly.

We are looking for someone who: works across disciplines (textile, movement, ceramics, poetry, cooking, etc.); blends art, hospitality, care, and community; feels comfortable in multilingual settings; is familiar with migration (by lived experience or affinity); can listen, let go, and stay open to the unexpected; prefers process over product; enjoys collaborating with people with no artistic training but strong imagination.

We especially welcome applications from artists with migration backgrounds, artists of color, queer, neurodiverse, and non-binary artists.",20 Nov 2025,2025-11-20,2026-09-23 12:37:25.444678+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_77d04e963291,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/dingen-die-niet-verkopen-verkopen-u-dingen/,https://www.dingendienietverkopen.be/calls,Dingen die niet verkopen,"We want to extend this theme to our annual group exhibition, ‘Dingen die niet verkopen, verkopen u dingen’, which will run from December 11th to December 21st of 2025. At a time when reality is stranger than fiction, we’re looking for visual art that actively explores the friction between truth and make-believe. For the occasion, we’re opening a department store stocked with untruths.",visual art,open call,Belgium,Antwerp,"We do not take ownership of your work, and you receive the full amount as agreed upon if sold. We will add an additional 20% to the sales price to cover the costs and communication of this exhibition, which we keep.",,,en,Open call Dingen die niet verkopen (‘Stuff that does not sell’),"We are looking for unique objects and/or editions/multiples that tell a false or distorted narrative through text or image. Three-dimensional works and objects, as well as zines and alternative forms of publication, are eligible. We prefer objects that can be displayed on a shelf, newspaper carousel, or table. Works intended for wall mounting are not eligible. Specifics: Your work tells a (fictional) story through text and/or image. We are looking for small works: you can hold them in one hand and they cost no more than €100 (including VAT).",Open call Dingen die niet verkopen (‘Stuff that does not sell’),"We are looking for unique objects and/or editions/multiples that tell a false or distorted narrative through text or image. Three-dimensional works and objects, as well as zines and alternative forms of publication, are eligible. We prefer objects that can be displayed on a shelf, newspaper carousel, or table. Works intended for wall mounting are not eligible. Specifics: Your work tells a (fictional) story through text and/or image. We are looking for small works: you can hold them in one hand and they cost no more than €100 (including VAT).",16 Nov 2025,2025-11-16,2026-09-23 12:37:25.448390+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_85c853ed4180,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/novi-sad-theatre-festival-2026-call-for-performances-for-children-and-young-people-serbia/,https://www.festivalnpi.co.rs/en/festival2024/news/open-call-novi-sad-thatre-festival-2026,"Youth Theatre, Novi Sad","Youth Theatre, Novi Sad, has opened the call for the 5th International Theatre Festival for Children and Youth, which will take place in the second week of May 2026. Professional theatres from around the world are invited to apply with performances for children and young people across all genres – from drama and puppetry to dance, shadow and object theatre. All types of theatre creation for children and youth are represented at the Festival.",Theatre,Call,Serbia,Novi Sad,"the organiser of the festival, provides accommodation and food for the participants as well as travel expenses in the total amount up to 2,000 EUR.",,,en,Novi Sad Theatre Festival 2026 Call for Performances for Children and Young People (Serbia),"Professional theatres from around the world are invited to apply with performances for children and young people across all genres – from drama and puppetry to dance, shadow and object theatre.",Novi Sad Theatre Festival 2026 Call for Performances for Children and Young People (Serbia),"Professional theatres from around the world are invited to apply with performances for children and young people across all genres – from drama and puppetry to dance, shadow and object theatre.",15 Nov 2025,2025-11-15,2026-09-23 12:37:25.451952+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_6aad32a7d163,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/werkgroep-advies-module-startende-kunstenaars/,,Kunstenpunt / Flanders Arts Institute,"Through this open call, we want to put together an external working group that will thoroughly review the module for starting artists, gather feedback, and provide input for its rewriting.","visual arts, performing arts, and/or classical music",open call,Belgium,null,We offer you compensation of €850 excluding VAT for the entire process. Train tickets will be reimbursed.,null,starting artists / emerging artists,en,Working group advice: module for starting artists,"You are active in the visual arts, performing arts, and/or classical music. You are not (or no longer) studying. Or you did not follow the traditional path of art education as an artist. You are at the start of your professional career – regardless of age – or you still have vivid memories of what it was like to be a starting artist. Or you have experience in supporting or guiding artists who are at the start of their professional careers. Or you are experiencing social barriers to starting your career. Due to their underrepresentation in the arts, we want to encourage everyone of color, women, people with disabilities or neurodivergence, members of the LGBTQIA+ community, and individuals who experience financial barriers to participate.",Working group advice: module for starting artists,"You are active in the visual arts, performing arts, and/or classical music. You are not (or no longer) studying. Or you did not follow the traditional path of art education as an artist. You are at the start of your professional career – regardless of age – or you still have vivid memories of what it was like to be a starting artist. Or you have experience in supporting or guiding artists who are at the start of their professional careers. Or you are experiencing social barriers to starting your career. Due to their underrepresentation in the arts, we want to encourage everyone of color, women, people with disabilities or neurodivergence, members of the LGBTQIA+ community, and individuals who experience financial barriers to participate.",14 Nov 2025,2025-11-14,2026-09-23 12:37:25.455479+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_937443956cc9,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/art-explora-cite-internationale-des-arts-residency-programme-2026/,https://artexplora.plateformecandidature.com/,Art Explora,"Art Explora, the international foundation that fosters new encounters between arts and audiences, locally, nationally and internationally, is pleased to announce that the call for applications for the Art Explora – Cité internationale des Arts Residency Programme 2026 is now open. Until October 31st 2025 , artists and collectives of artists, researchers and curators from all around the world are invited to apply for this unique residency programme, with projects that question relations between art, science and technology, and address social and ecological issues of our time.","artists, researchers and curators",Residency,Albania,Tirana,"All residents benefit from a fully-furnished studio for 3 or 6 months, production and living grants. ... each year, two artists hosted within the Art Explora Residencies will also benefit from access to Lafayette Anticipations’ production workshops, additional support and a production budget of up to €3,000.",,,en,Art Explora – Cité internationale des arts Residency programme 2026,"artists and collectives of artists, researchers and curators from all around the world are invited to apply for this unique residency programme, with projects that question relations between art, science and technology, and address social and ecological issues of our time.",Art Explora – Cité internationale des arts Residency programme 2026,"artists and collectives of artists, researchers and curators from all around the world are invited to apply for this unique residency programme, with projects that question relations between art, science and technology, and address social and ecological issues of our time.","Applications are open until October 30th, 2025, 11:59pm (GMT+02:00, Europe/Paris)",2025-10-30,2026-09-23 12:37:25.460869+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_c38ccf84a460,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-cinema-canape/,https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeLTGOleELcKlPxI-kfUjgBmHpKCFaJ5kUl_wfanYvPmVnZag/viewform,Call Canapé vzw,"CINEMA CANAPÉ is always looking for people who want to share their work! This open call will serve as a database. So don’t worry if we don’t reach out to you right away, we’ll keep your submission and contact artists who fit upcoming screenings. Whether you’re working on short film, experimental video, documentary, animation, or something in between: all forms and genres are welcome. No experience needed (but very welcome) we want to create an open space for experimentation, trying things out, and sharing with others. Our upcoming curation has a special focus on the spooky, mysterious, and dark","filmmakers, video artists, and moving-image makers",open call,,,,,,en,Open call Cinema Canapé,"This call is especially for all filmmakers, video artists, and moving-image makers. Whether you’re working on short film, experimental video, documentary, animation, or something in between: all forms and genres are welcome. No experience needed (but very welcome)",Open call Cinema Canapé,"This call is especially for all filmmakers, video artists, and moving-image makers. Whether you’re working on short film, experimental video, documentary, animation, or something in between: all forms and genres are welcome. No experience needed (but very welcome)",20 Oct 2025,2025-10-20,2026-09-23 12:37:25.464190+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_0b695cd43d60,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/invitation-for-members/,https://forms.gle/7gLeM6zVynQNyqBB9,DomestiCity,"DomestiCity is a socially engaged artist-run space based in Laken, Brussels. We open up the basement of our house for neighbours, friends, passerby for artistic and reflective activities and events linked to craft – slowing down – working together – dialogue. In 2025 we will reshape the collective into a living (room) library where we gather and pass on (embodied) knowledge about crafts – commonism – micro-politics.",craft,Call,Belgium,Brussels,,,,en,Invitation for Members*,"Housemate/member : You participate in the project from within the house. You join meetings and engage with the public gatherings in our basement twice a month. You give input in the gatherings- what would you like to do? You help to shape the always-evolving collective.You live in our house and can use the project space as a collective atelier/work space. (If you want more info about the house (democratic rent, photos, housemates) or would like to visit it, please contact domesticitybrussels@gmail.com

Participative member : You engage with the public gatherings in our basement twice a month (+-8h per month). You give input in the gatherings – what would you like to do? You can use the project space as a collective atelier/working space. You help to shape the always-evolving collective.

Volunteer : You would like to help out with one of the gatherings that interests you. On this link , you can find more information about the specific questions we would like to have an answer on.",Invitation for Members*,"Housemate/member : You participate in the project from within the house. You join meetings and engage with the public gatherings in our basement twice a month. You give input in the gatherings- what would you like to do? You help to shape the always-evolving collective.You live in our house and can use the project space as a collective atelier/work space. (If you want more info about the house (democratic rent, photos, housemates) or would like to visit it, please contact domesticitybrussels@gmail.com

Participative member : You engage with the public gatherings in our basement twice a month (+-8h per month). You give input in the gatherings – what would you like to do? You can use the project space as a collective atelier/working space. You help to shape the always-evolving collective.

Volunteer : You would like to help out with one of the gatherings that interests you. On this link , you can find more information about the specific questions we would like to have an answer on.",12 Oct 2025,2025-10-12,2026-09-23 12:37:25.467257+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_6f9b625b869d,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/word-een-rema-member/,https://www.rema-eemn.net/join-us/,REMA,"By becoming a REMA member, you can take part in all REMA events and boost your own activities!",early music,membership call for applications,,,,,,en,Become REMA member,"Since 25 May 2023, REMA has been open to all types of early music players (ensembles, festivals, concert halls, research institutes, labels, agents, conservatoires, etc.). There is only one way to join REMA: each year, a call for applications enables around thirty new organisations to join the REMA network. In 2025, applications are open from 1 July to 8 October: new members will be welcomed on 1 January 2026. The 2026 General Assembly will be held in Malta from 20 to 22 January 2026. CRITERIA FOR JOINING Applicant organisations must have been in existence for a minimum of three years and possess a legal entity status. The Board of Directors will look at: The overall quality of the activities The alignment of the applicants’ values with REMA The criteria and selection process are detailed in the full call. You will be asked to: Provide information about your organisation. Select a main activity: promoter, ensemble, education, research, agent, publisher or other. Once accepted, members can represent all their activities. Answer specific questions related to your main activity and submit relevant documentation (e.g. programme of activities, list of publications, concerts, etc.) Explain your motivation for joining REMA and how your values are in line with the network. Submit a letter of recommendation from a REMA member. Additional information: if you have taken part in a network project in the past, include this information in your application. CODE OF CONDUCT From the moment they apply, all candidates must endorse the network’s code of conduct, established with the members, which ensures adherence to professional ethics among REMA members. The code of conduct delineates the expected or unlawful or inappropriate behavior from members, and outlines the procedure for penalizing such conduct.",Become REMA member,"Since 25 May 2023, REMA has been open to all types of early music players (ensembles, festivals, concert halls, research institutes, labels, agents, conservatoires, etc.). There is only one way to join REMA: each year, a call for applications enables around thirty new organisations to join the REMA network. In 2025, applications are open from 1 July to 8 October: new members will be welcomed on 1 January 2026. The 2026 General Assembly will be held in Malta from 20 to 22 January 2026. CRITERIA FOR JOINING Applicant organisations must have been in existence for a minimum of three years and possess a legal entity status. The Board of Directors will look at: The overall quality of the activities The alignment of the applicants’ values with REMA The criteria and selection process are detailed in the full call. You will be asked to: Provide information about your organisation. Select a main activity: promoter, ensemble, education, research, agent, publisher or other. Once accepted, members can represent all their activities. Answer specific questions related to your main activity and submit relevant documentation (e.g. programme of activities, list of publications, concerts, etc.) Explain your motivation for joining REMA and how your values are in line with the network. Submit a letter of recommendation from a REMA member. Additional information: if you have taken part in a network project in the past, include this information in your application. CODE OF CONDUCT From the moment they apply, all candidates must endorse the network’s code of conduct, established with the members, which ensures adherence to professional ethics among REMA members. The code of conduct delineates the expected or unlawful or inappropriate behavior from members, and outlines the procedure for penalizing such conduct.",08 Oct 2025,2025-10-08,2026-09-23 12:37:25.470611+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_a5a634ac992c,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/gezocht-belgische-fotografen-voor-nieuwe-tentoonstelling-bij-hangar/,https://www.hangar.art/open-call2025,Hangar,"As part of the bicentenary celebration (September 2026 to September 2027) of le Point de vue du gras* , considered the first photographic image in world history, the Centre national des arts plastiques (CNAP) in France has commissioned 15 photographers, focusing on the invention of photography and the relevance of its possible reinvention today. The projects are created using all the techniques that currently allow artists to produce photographic images in innovative forms. Hangar, one of the certified venues of the bicentenary celebration, will host the exhibition of the 15 projects from this commission in September 2026 on the theme “Reinventing Photography”. To complement this exhibition, Hangar has decided to launch a call for applications open to Belgian artists photographers and/or artists photographers residing in Belgium . This call invites artists photographers to explore the same theme: 200 years later, how can photography be reinvented? Is photography a medium that reinvents itself? How do photographic artists, through their practice, keep contemporary photography alive? The call for applications will constitute the Belgian part of the exhibition.",photography,open call,Belgium,null,Support for the production costs of the exhibition’s works. Cash prize of 4000€ for each of 5 laureates.,,,en,Open Call: Reinventing Photography by Hangar,"Conditions for participation being over the age of majority (18+) being a Belgian artist photographer and/or artists photographers residing in Belgium should demonstrate at least ONE of these two possibilities: – have a track record of professional practice as an artist (exhibitions, publications) – have an art school degree This call is open ONLY for original and unpublished projects / The works must be conceived, created, and produced specifically for this commission and presented for the first time at Hangar.",Open Call: Reinventing Photography by Hangar,"Conditions for participation being over the age of majority (18+) being a Belgian artist photographer and/or artists photographers residing in Belgium should demonstrate at least ONE of these two possibilities: – have a track record of professional practice as an artist (exhibitions, publications) – have an art school degree This call is open ONLY for original and unpublished projects / The works must be conceived, created, and produced specifically for this commission and presented for the first time at Hangar.",03 Oct 2025,2025-10-03,2026-09-23 12:37:25.473521+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_655be783ebe9,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/belgian-photo-awards-2025/,https://belgianphotoawards.com/,Belgian Photo Awards,"The Belgian Photo Awards honor professional photography talent in Belgium, with awards in a variety of categories: from portrait and documentary to wedding photography and commercial assignments.",photography,competition,Belgium,Leuven,,,emerging talent (18-35),en,Belgian Photo Awards 2025,"The Belgian Photo Awards honor professional photography talent in Belgium, with awards in a variety of categories: from portrait and documentary to wedding photography and commercial assignments.",Belgian Photo Awards 2025,"The Belgian Photo Awards honor professional photography talent in Belgium, with awards in a variety of categories: from portrait and documentary to wedding photography and commercial assignments.",10 Sep 2025,2025-09-10,2026-09-23 12:37:25.478023+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_75741deaac9b,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/goddessarts-prize-open-call/,https://www.goddessartsmag.com/goddessarts-prize,Goddessarts Magazine,"We are thrilled to announce our first art prize, celebrating the divine feminine in all her forms – from mythological figures to mothers, muses, spiritual archetypes, and women who inspire. This is your moment to channel your vision of what a goddess means to you! All mediums welcome – painting, sculpture, drawing, collage, photography, mixed media & digital art.","All mediums welcome – painting, sculpture, drawing, collage, photography, mixed media & digital art.",Art Prize Competition,international,,"1st Prize: 250 € Cash, Solo Virtual Exhibition, 6-page Magazine Feature, Interview, Winner’s Certificate",Early Bird – July 20 | Fee: 35 € Regular – August 31 | Fee: 45 €,artist of all stages of career and all ages,en,Goddessarts Prize – Open Call,"Eligibility: international, artist of all stages of career and all ages",Goddessarts Prize – Open Call,"Eligibility: international, artist of all stages of career and all ages",31 Aug 2025,2025-08-31,2026-09-23 12:37:25.481413+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_437b564efaf9,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/residentie-bij-khmessen-noorwegen/,http://www.khmessen.no/,Kunstnarhuset Messen,"Applications are now open for a working period for 1- to 3 months in 2026 at International Art residency KHMessen in Norway! A beautiful residency that is located in the hart of the Hardanger, between the mountains and the fjord. The Art residence gives time for reflection, research, presentation and production.","visual artists, writers, composer/musicians, performance artists",Residency,Norway,Ålvik,,we ask a fee of 1000 Norwegian Krone per month (approx. 85 euro).,at any stage of their careers,en,Residency at KHMessen (Noorwegen),"We welcome visual artists, writers, composer/musicians, performance artists at any stage of their careers who are interested in exploring and expanding their work in a unique and supportive environment.",Residency at KHMessen (Noorwegen),"We welcome visual artists, writers, composer/musicians, performance artists at any stage of their careers who are interested in exploring and expanding their work in a unique and supportive environment.",31 Aug 2025,2025-08-31,2026-09-23 12:37:25.485019+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_e7ad5b0af54f,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/open-call-voor-residentie-silence-awareness-existence-in-finland/,https://www.arteles.org,Arteles Creative Center,"Thematic, transdisciplinary residency program in Finland for artists, writers, researchers and creative minds attuned to the theme. The program brings together creative individuals from different backgrounds. Artistic, scientific, meditative and existentialistic approaches are all equally embraced. Taking place at the heart of the Northern winter, the conditions are excellent for creative contemplation, solitary introspection, concentrating intensively on your work, thinking and being, as well as for sharing experiences and ideas with other, similarly oriented minds. There is no pressure to have a concrete productive outcome, in case your focus is more in inner development, self-reflection and research. All participation in group activities is voluntary.","artists, writers, researchers",Residency,Finland,,"Applicants who otherwise would be unable to join the program can apply for financial support. The number of financially supported residencies is limited. Regular fee: 1950 € / monthly period Financially supported fee (limited availability): 1350 € / monthly period Contributor’s fee (optional): 2610 € / monthly period All fees include the registration fee (120 € / person, non-refundable, to be paid only if/when becoming selected). All the residents have accommodation in a private bedroom.",There is no application fee.,,en,Open Call for residency Silence Awareness Existence in Finland,"Thematic, transdisciplinary residency program in Finland for artists, writers, researchers and creative minds attuned to the theme. The program brings together creative individuals from different backgrounds. Artistic, scientific, meditative and existentialistic approaches are all equally embraced.",Open Call for residency Silence Awareness Existence in Finland,"Thematic, transdisciplinary residency program in Finland for artists, writers, researchers and creative minds attuned to the theme. The program brings together creative individuals from different backgrounds. Artistic, scientific, meditative and existentialistic approaches are all equally embraced.",28 Aug 2025,2025-08-28,2026-09-23 12:37:25.488378+00:00
kunsten_be_flanders_29113af76b09,kunsten_be_flanders,https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/call-for-applications-curators-workshop-for-early-career-curators-educators-and-other-practitioners-on-the-occasion-of-the-13th-berlin-biennale-for-contemporary-art/,https://newslettertogo.com/rimnoamr-ewuq4wja-l61ez4k6-ull,Berlin Biennale,"Marking its 10th iteration since 2006, this edition of the Curators Workshop Fugitive Acts: Art and Politics considers the place of politics within contemporary exhibition making.","curators, educators, and other practitioners",workshop,Germany,Berlin,with the support of 13th Berlin Biennale’s Educational Partner Volkswagen Group,,early-career,en,Call for Applications: Curators Workshop on the occasion of the 13th Berlin Biennale for Contemporary Art,"the Berlin Biennale invites a group of fifteen early-career curators, educators, and other practitioners to participate in this seven-day workshop.",Call for Applications: Curators Workshop on the occasion of the 13th Berlin Biennale for Contemporary Art,"the Berlin Biennale invites a group of fifteen early-career curators, educators, and other practitioners to participate in this seven-day workshop.",13 Jul 2025,2025-07-13,2026-09-23 12:37:25.491320+00:00
kunststiftung_nrw_efc250f36f03,kunststiftung_nrw,https://www.kunststiftungnrw.de/visuelle-kunst/foerderung/auftakt/,https://www.kunststiftungnrw.de/visuelle-kunst/foerderung/auftakt/antrag-auftakt/,Kunststiftung NRW,"Mit dem Förderprogramm AUFTAKT unterstützen wir die Umsetzung künstlerischer Vorhaben, Produktionen, Publikationen und vergeben Recherche-, Auslands- und Arbeitsstipendien für Kunstschaffende am Anfang ihrer Karriere.",Visuelle Kunst,Förderprogramm,Nordrhein-Westfalen,,,,Kunstschaffende am Anfang ihrer Karriere,de,AUFTAKT,Kunstschaffende am Anfang ihrer Karriere und unabhängige Projekträume können ihre Anträge über das Antragsverfahren AUFTAKT einreichen.,OPENING,Artists at the beginning of their career and independent project spaces can submit their applications via the AUFTAKT application process.,,,2026-09-23 12:37:26.426103+00:00
kunststiftung_nrw_b80457c32c17,kunststiftung_nrw,https://www.kunststiftungnrw.de/visuelle-kunst/foerderung/stipendien/arbeits-und-recherchestipendien/,https://www.kunststiftungnrw.de/visuelle-kunst/foerderung/stipendien/arbeits-und-recherchestipendien/antrag-arbeits-und-recherchestipendien/,Kunststiftung NRW,"Die Kunststiftung NRW unterst␀fctzt professionelle K␀fcnstler:innen sowie Institutionen und Initiativen aus Nordrhein-Westfalen, deren Arbeiten durch k␀fcnstlerische Vielfalt, hohe Qualit␀e4t und besondere Relevanz ␀fcberzeugen.",Visuelle Kunst,Stipendien,Nordrhein-Westfalen,,,,Kunstschaffende am Anfang ihrer Karriere,de,Arbeits- und Recherchestipendien,Kunstschaffende am Anfang ihrer Karriere und unabh␀e4ngige Projektr␀e4ume k␀f6nnen ihre Antr␀e4ge ␀fcber das Antragsverfahren AUFTAKT einreichen.,Work and research scholarships,Artists at the beginning of their careers and independent project spaces can submit their applications via the AUFTAKT application process.,,,2026-09-23 12:37:27.298285+00:00
kunststiftung_nrw_d141b3d73058,kunststiftung_nrw,https://www.kunststiftungnrw.de/visuelle-kunst/foerderung/stipendien/reisestipendien-spotlight-polen/,https://www.kunststiftungnrw.de/visuelle-kunst/foerderung/stipendien/reisestipendien-spotlight-polen/vergabemodalitaeten-polen-vk/,Kunststiftung NRW,"Mit dem ""Spotlight""-Programm ermöglicht die Kunststiftung NRW künstlerisch oder kuratorisch arbeitenden Personen Aufenthalte in Polen. Beantragt werden können wahlweise vier bzw. sechswöchige Reisestipendien. Die Planung und Umsetzung wird eigenständig übernommen. Sie können die Zeit nutzen, um eine konzentrierte Recherche vorzunehmen oder künstlerische Kontakte aufzubauen und zu vertiefen.",Visuelle Kunst,Stipendien,Polen,,"Einzelpersonen können eine Förderung von bis zu 7.500 Euro beantragen, künstlerische Duos bis zu 15.000 Euro.",,,de,Reisestipendien / Spotlight Polen,"Voraussetzung für Ihre Bewerbung ist, dass Sie bereits erste Verbindungen zu Akteur:innen oder Institutionen vor Ort aufgenommen haben, mit denen Sie zusammenarbeiten möchten.",Travel grants / Spotlight Poland,A prerequisite for your application is that you have already established initial contacts with actors or institutions on site with whom you would like to work together.,,,2026-09-23 12:37:28.100243+00:00
kunststiftung_nrw_13b9c46310b0,kunststiftung_nrw,https://www.kunststiftungnrw.de/visuelle-kunst/foerderung/residenzen/atelier-galata-istanbul/,https://www.kunststiftungnrw.de/visuelle-kunst/foerderung/residenzen/atelier-galata-istanbul/atelier-galata-visuelle-kunst/,Kunststiftung NRW,"Die Kunststiftung NRW vergibt ein Residenzstipendium im Bereich Visuelle Kunst in Istanbul. Ziel des Stipendiums ist es, die Kunstszene vor Ort kennenzulernen, Kontakte zu knüpfen, Ideen auszutauschen und diese Impulse später nach in ihre jeweiligen ihre Arbeitskontexte in Nordrhein-Westfalen einzubringen.",Visuelle Kunst,Residenzstipendium,"NRW, Istanbul",Istanbul,,,professionelle Kunstschaffende ... die bereits öffentliche Anerkennung erfahren haben und erste Berufserfolge vorweisen können,de,"Atelier Galata, Istanbul","Die Ausschreibung ist nicht alterslimitiert. Sie richtet sich an professionelle Kunstschaffende mit Lebensmittelpunkt in Nordrhein-Westfalen, die bereits öffentliche Anerkennung erfahren haben und erste Berufserfolge vorweisen können.","Atelier Galata, Istanbul","The call is not age-limited. It is aimed at professional artists whose center of life is in North Rhine-Westphalia, who have already received public recognition and can demonstrate initial professional successes.",,,2026-09-23 12:37:29.481852+00:00
kunststiftung_nrw_9fcfea3c0364,kunststiftung_nrw,https://www.kunststiftungnrw.de/visuelle-kunst/stiftungsinitiativen/residence-nrw/,https://www.residencenrw.de/de/ausschreibung/,Kunststiftung NRW,Stipendien für bildende Künstler:innen und Kurator:innen an einem gemeinsamen Residenzort in Münster,bildende Kunst,Stipendien,Deutschland,Münster,,,besonders begabte junge Kunstschaffende,de,Residence NRW+,ein Programm für besonders begabte junge Kunstschaffende der bildenden Gegenwartskunst. Pro Jahr werden vier zwölfmonatige Stipe,Residence NRW+,a program for particularly gifted young visual artists in contemporary art. Four twelve-month stipends are awarded each year.,,,2026-09-23 12:37:31.247247+00:00
kunststiftung_nrw_72dbd2a3195b,kunststiftung_nrw,https://www.residencenrw.de/de/ausschreibung/,,Residence NRW⁺,"Residence NRW⁺ richtet sich an bildende Künstler:innen und
                Kurator:innen mit Bezug zum Bundesland Nordrhein-Westfalen
                sowie an Kurator:innen aus der Schweiz. Mit den vier
                programmatischen Kernelementen – Austausch, Praxis, Betreuung
                und Netzwerk – bietet Residence NRW⁺ die bestmöglichen
                Bedingungen für die Weiterentwicklung im jeweiligen
                Arbeitsfeld. Pro Jahr vergibt Residence NRW⁺ vier zwölfmonatige Stipendien für
                bildende Künstler:innen sowie vier sechsmonatige Stipendien für
                Kurator:innen.",bildende Künstler:innen; Kurator:innen,Stipendium,Deutschland,Schloss Ringenberg,"Die monatliche Stipendienzuwendung beträgt 1.700 Euro (1.500 Euro Lebenshaltung, 200 Euro Produktionskostenzuschuss).",,,de,Residence NRW⁺ Ausschreibung,"Residence NRW⁺ richtet sich an bildende Künstler:innen und
                Kurator:innen mit Bezug zum Bundesland Nordrhein-Westfalen
                sowie an Kurator:innen aus der Schweiz.

Residence NRW⁺ richtet sich an Künstler:innen mit Bezug zum
                Bundeland Nordrhein-Westfalen (Herkunft, Studium oder
                Wohn-/Arbeitsort). Erforderlich ist ein abgeschlossenes Studium
                an einer Kunstakademie/Kunsthochschule. Der Abschluss der
                künstlerischen Ausbildung der Stipendiat:innen darf bei Antritt
                des Stipendiums nicht länger als fünf Jahre zurückliegen oder
                die Stipendiat:innen dürfen nicht älter als 40 Jahre sein. Die
                Stipendienzeit vornehmlich am Residenzort zu verbringen und an
                gemeinsamen Veranstaltungen (Arbeitstreffen, Exkursionen,
                Eröffnungen, etc.) teilzunehmen, sind verpflichtend.

Residence NRW⁺ richtet sich an Kurator:innen mit Bezug zum
                Bundesland Nordrhein-Westfalen bzw. der Schweiz, die profunde
                Kenntnisse im Bereich der zeitgenössischen Kunst besitzen und
                bereits eine eigene Vorstellung der kuratorischen Arbeit
                entwickelt haben sowie Gelegenheit hatten, erste Projekte zu
                realisieren. Voraussetzung ist die Bereitschaft, die
                Stipendienzeit vornehmlich am Residenzort zu verbringen und an
                gemeinsamen Veranstaltungen (Arbeitstreffen, Exkursionen,
                Eröffnungen etc.) teilzunehmen. Bewerber:innen mit Bezug zum
                Bundesland NRW müssen ein Universitätsstudium (Master, Diplom,
                Magister oder Promotion; Kunstgeschichte, Kunst,
                Kulturwissenschaften oder ähnliches) abgeschlossen haben;
                ferner gilt, dass ihr Studienabschluss bei Antritt des
                Stipendiums nicht länger als fünf Jahre zurückliegt oder sie
                nicht älter als 35 Jahre sein dürfen. Für Bewerber:innen mit
                Bezug zur Schweiz gilt kein Alterslimit, jedoch darf auch hier
                der Abschluss der Ausbildung oder, falls keine Ausbildung
                vorliegt, die erste öffentliche Präsentation der kuratorischen
                Arbeit nicht länger als 5 Jahre zurückliegen.",Residence NRW⁺ Call for Applications,"Residence NRW⁺ is aimed at visual artists and curators with a connection to the federal state of North Rhine-Westphalia as well as curators from Switzerland.

Residence NRW⁺ is aimed at artists with a connection to the federal state of North Rhine-Westphalia (origin, studies, or place of residence/work). A completed degree from an academy of art/university of the arts is required. At the start of the scholarship, the completion of the artistic training of the scholarship recipients must not be more than five years in the past, or the scholarship recipients must not be older than 40 years. It is mandatory to spend the scholarship period primarily at the residence location and to participate in joint events (work meetings, excursions, openings, etc.).

Residence NRW⁺ is aimed at curators with a connection to the federal state of North Rhine-Westphalia or Switzerland who have in-depth knowledge in the field of contemporary art and have already developed their own conception of curatorial work as well as had the opportunity to realize initial projects. A prerequisite is the willingness to spend the scholarship period primarily at the residence location and to participate in joint events (work meetings, excursions, openings, etc.). Applicants with a connection to the federal state of NRW must have completed a university degree (Master, Diplom, Magister, or doctorate; art history, art, cultural studies, or similar); furthermore, their degree must not be more than five years old at the start of the scholarship, or they must not be older than 35 years. For applicants with a connection to Switzerland, there is no age limit; however, here too the completion of the training or, if no training exists, the first public presentation of the curatorial work must not be more than 5 years in the past.",,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.005512+00:00
matadero_madrid_15564c0bdd34,matadero_madrid,https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/calls/open-call-situated-research-residencies-2027,https://eu.jotform.com/241562142081346,Medialab Matadero,"We are looking for proposals that sit at the margins or intersections of disciplines, methodologies, and ‘knowledges’. Inspired by the principle of learning by doing, the residency aims to foster new ways of researching, prototyping, documenting, sharing knowledge, or mobilizing communities around relevant issues.","design, art, architecture, urbanism, economics, film, photography, journalism, digital media, environmental science, philosophy, engineering, social studies, political science, programming, materials science, activism",residency,Spain,Madrid,"carries a stipend of €10,000 (before tax)",,emerging profiles,en,Open Call for Situated Research Residencies 2027,"For individuals or collectives researching in the fields of design, art, architecture, urbanism, economics, film, photography, journalism, digital media, environmental science, philosophy, engineering, social studies, political science, programming, materials science, activism, or any other field consistent with the stated goals. We will value each applicant's particular trajectory, with the aim of fostering exchange between expert and emerging profiles.",Open Call for Situated Research Residencies 2027,"For individuals or collectives researching in the fields of design, art, architecture, urbanism, economics, film, photography, journalism, digital media, environmental science, philosophy, engineering, social studies, political science, programming, materials science, activism, or any other field consistent with the stated goals. We will value each applicant's particular trajectory, with the aim of fostering exchange between expert and emerging profiles.","September 27, 2026, 11:59PM",2026-09-27,2026-09-23 12:37:34.013419+00:00
matadero_madrid_9e814c5cf987,matadero_madrid,https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/calls/open-call-lab-5-mechanics-truth,https://form.jotform.com/251244533209350,Matadero Madrid / Medialab Matadero,"Medialab Matadero invites project proposals and multidisciplinary collaborators for the Collaborative Prototyping Lab (LPC) , a two-week residency in the framework of the annual thematic program LAB 5 The Mechanics of Truth .","visual cultures, technologies and digital media, architecture and urbanism, writing, journalism, social studies, activism, science, engineering, economics",residency,Spain,Madrid,A workspace and tools will be provided for the development of each project.,"No, participation is free.",both at early stages and in more established phases of their professional careers.,en,Open Call - LAB 5 The Mechanics of Truth,"This call is aimed both at people who want to propose one of the five projects to be developed and at those who want to join as collaborators in developing them. The LPC is open to people with experience or training in visual cultures, technologies and digital media, architecture and urbanism, writing, journalism, social studies, activism, science, engineering, economics, and any other field that can connect with one or more of the themes of LAB 5 The Mechanics of Truth. Applicants must be 18 years or older. Other than that, we welcome anyone to apply, regardless of origin or place of residence.",Open Call - LAB 5 The Mechanics of Truth,"This call is aimed both at people who want to propose one of the five projects to be developed and at those who want to join as collaborators in developing them. The LPC is open to people with experience or training in visual cultures, technologies and digital media, architecture and urbanism, writing, journalism, social studies, activism, science, engineering, economics, and any other field that can connect with one or more of the themes of LAB 5 The Mechanics of Truth. Applicants must be 18 years or older. Other than that, we welcome anyone to apply, regardless of origin or place of residence.","June 14, 2026",2026-06-14,2026-09-23 12:37:34.017602+00:00
matadero_madrid_eef852af4ca0,matadero_madrid,https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/calls/open-call-projects-lab-4-weird-futures,https://form.jotform.com/251244533209350,Medialab Matadero,"Medialab Matadero is seeking proposals for the Collaborative Prototyping Lab, a creative residency in the framework of the year-long LAB 4 Weird Futures programme",contemporary art and design research,creative residency,Spain,Madrid,"We will cover travel and accommodation costs for those selected from outside Madrid during this period.

Medialab will also cover some production costs and provide technical support in areas defined in the full description rules of the call.",,both early and advanced stages of their careers,en,OPEN CALL FOR PROJECTS LAB 4 WEIRD FUTURES,"With this call we are looking for original and specific proposals that will allow us to explore the themes of the call from a wide range of perspectives. We will welcome applications from the fields of contemporary art and design research, at both early and advanced stages of their careers. We are also interested in proposals related to activism, writing, visual cultures and new visualities, performance, and with backgrounds as diverse as architecture, engineering, biology, economics, political science, and many more. In general, we are looking for experts (or future experts) on any of the themes of the LAB 4 Weird Futures programme who are interested in having an impact on the technological aspects of contemporary society and are willing to collaboratively test and expand specific proposals.

The Collaborative Prototyping Lab will take place at Medialab Matadero in Madrid from 12 to 27 November 2025 ...

Participation in the lab sessions must be in person and for the entire duration of the programme.",OPEN CALL FOR PROJECTS LAB 4 WEIRD FUTURES,"With this call we are looking for original and specific proposals that will allow us to explore the themes of the call from a wide range of perspectives. We will welcome applications from the fields of contemporary art and design research, at both early and advanced stages of their careers. We are also interested in proposals related to activism, writing, visual cultures and new visualities, performance, and with backgrounds as diverse as architecture, engineering, biology, economics, political science, and many more. In general, we are looking for experts (or future experts) on any of the themes of the LAB 4 Weird Futures programme who are interested in having an impact on the technological aspects of contemporary society and are willing to collaboratively test and expand specific proposals.

The Collaborative Prototyping Lab will take place at Medialab Matadero in Madrid from 12 to 27 November 2025 ...

Participation in the lab sessions must be in person and for the entire duration of the programme.",Until 15th June at 23:59h CET,2027-06-15,2026-09-23 12:37:34.025966+00:00
mondriaan_fund_8e2af8800941,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/acquisitions/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,Do you represent a museum or other heritage institution and wish to make an acquisition that would enrich the Dutch National Cultural Heritage Collection? This could range from contemporary art and crafts to ancient manuscripts and natural history collections. You may be eligible for an Acquisitions grant.,contemporary art and crafts to ancient manuscripts and natural history collections,grant,Dutch,,The maximum grant offered by the Mondriaan Fund is 40% of the estimated value of the acquisition.,,,en,Acquisitions,"For Dutch museums and other cultural heritage institutions.

The application procedure is open to publicly accessible Dutch institutions that are in charge of museum collections of national or international significance. When a museum submits an application, it is registered in the museum register. Grants cannot be used for acquisitions which institutions can be reasonably expected to fund from their regular budgets. Museums which receive an Acquisition Programs grant must explain in their applications why they are unable to fund the acquisition from their Acquisition Programs budget. If the intended acquisition comprises multiple objects, funding is only available if these objects constitute an inseparable ensemble. The application must include research into the provenance of the intended acquisition. If the provenance is incomplete, the application must also include an overview of all steps taken by the applicant to determine whether the object may have a problematic history, such as (potential) cases of looted art, unlawful acquisition or illegal export from the country of origin. Acquisitions grants cannot be used to fund constructional provisions, the preservation of listed buildings, the excavation of archaeological objects or passive conservation. Nor can they be used to document the institution’s collection. Grants0cannot be requested for the acquisition of artists’ estates. The estimated value of the object must exceed  50,000. This value must be substantiated by the valuation report provided, as specified in the checklist. The valuation must be carried out by an independent valuer who has no ties with the applying institution. The institution is accommodating in its lending practices with other Dutch institutions and follows the Slimmer Lenen guidelines, generally granting loan requests unless there are compelling reasons not to, such as concerns about security, climatic conditions or the object’s condition. Dutch museums are not charged loan fees. Direct costs, such as for transport, insurance and crating (handling fees) are kept as low as possible. If a loan is denied, the institution must provide a substantive explanation to the requesting party. The acquisition will remain part of the Dutch National Cultural Heritage Collection for a long time and its ownership will not be transferred without the Mondriaan Fund’s authorisation. The preservation of the acquired object will be safeguarded through proper constructional provisions, climate control and security measures. The applicant will make a significant financial contribution to the acquisition of the object itself. In principle, applications requesting more than  500,000 are submitted to the Ministry of Education, Culture and Science for a contribution from the Museum Acquisition Fund, unless the Board of the Mondriaan Fund decides otherwise. If you wish to apply for more than  500,000, always contact one of the grant officers for this scheme beforehand. Objects listed in the register of protected cultural heritage under the Cultural Heritage Preservation Act with a purchase price above ,000,000 are not eligible for an Acquisitions grant. For these, you should contact the Ministry of Education, Culture and Science directly. The applicant should provide a clear account of how the purchase price was established. This may include aspects such as: how was the market value determined? How was the final sum agreed upon? Were there negotiations on the purchase price, and what was the outcome? If the Mondriaan Fund chooses to appoint a representative of an auction house to the advisory committee, the museum will not be allowed to request an appraisal or countercheck from the same auction house. Privately owned museums can only apply for a grant if their articles of association state that their collection or the object concerned belongs to the publicly accessible Dutch National Cultural Heritage Collection. The acquisition will be displayed to the public at once or as soon as possible.",Acquisitions,"For Dutch museums and other cultural heritage institutions.

The application procedure is open to publicly accessible Dutch institutions that are in charge of museum collections of national or international significance. When a museum submits an application, it is registered in the museum register. Grants cannot be used for acquisitions which institutions can be reasonably expected to fund from their regular budgets. Museums which receive an Acquisition Programs grant must explain in their applications why they are unable to fund the acquisition from their Acquisition Programs budget. If the intended acquisition comprises multiple objects, funding is only available if these objects constitute an inseparable ensemble. The application must include research into the provenance of the intended acquisition. If the provenance is incomplete, the application must also include an overview of all steps taken by the applicant to determine whether the object may have a problematic history, such as (potential) cases of looted art, unlawful acquisition or illegal export from the country of origin. Acquisitions grants cannot be used to fund constructional provisions, the preservation of listed buildings, the excavation of archaeological objects or passive conservation. Nor can they be used to document the institution’s collection. Grants0cannot be requested for the acquisition of artists’ estates. The estimated value of the object must exceed  50,000. This value must be substantiated by the valuation report provided, as specified in the checklist. The valuation must be carried out by an independent valuer who has no ties with the applying institution. The institution is accommodating in its lending practices with other Dutch institutions and follows the Slimmer Lenen guidelines, generally granting loan requests unless there are compelling reasons not to, such as concerns about security, climatic conditions or the object’s condition. Dutch museums are not charged loan fees. Direct costs, such as for transport, insurance and crating (handling fees) are kept as low as possible. If a loan is denied, the institution must provide a substantive explanation to the requesting party. The acquisition will remain part of the Dutch National Cultural Heritage Collection for a long time and its ownership will not be transferred without the Mondriaan Fund’s authorisation. The preservation of the acquired object will be safeguarded through proper constructional provisions, climate control and security measures. The applicant will make a significant financial contribution to the acquisition of the object itself. In principle, applications requesting more than  500,000 are submitted to the Ministry of Education, Culture and Science for a contribution from the Museum Acquisition Fund, unless the Board of the Mondriaan Fund decides otherwise. If you wish to apply for more than  500,000, always contact one of the grant officers for this scheme beforehand. Objects listed in the register of protected cultural heritage under the Cultural Heritage Preservation Act with a purchase price above ,000,000 are not eligible for an Acquisitions grant. For these, you should contact the Ministry of Education, Culture and Science directly. The applicant should provide a clear account of how the purchase price was established. This may include aspects such as: how was the market value determined? How was the final sum agreed upon? Were there negotiations on the purchase price, and what was the outcome? If the Mondriaan Fund chooses to appoint a representative of an auction house to the advisory committee, the museum will not be allowed to request an appraisal or countercheck from the same auction house. Privately owned museums can only apply for a grant if their articles of association state that their collection or the object concerned belongs to the publicly accessible Dutch National Cultural Heritage Collection. The acquisition will be displayed to the public at once or as soon as possible.",Continuous,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.026439+00:00
mondriaan_fund_3afe43141b61,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/art-commission/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,"Do you want to commission an artist to create new work or works that will be visible to everyone, in a publicly accessible space, for example in a hospital, museum or shopping centre? Or would you like to establish a partnership or supportive collaboration with an artist? If so, you may be eligible for an Art Commission grant from the Mondriaan Fund.",visual arts,grant,the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom,,The amount of the stipend is individually determined for each application.,,,en,Art Commission,"Anyone without intention to sell the work can commission visual artists to create new works of art accessible to the public in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.

Anyone can apply, except for individual artists, art education institutions, post-graduate institutions and predominantly sales-oriented commercial art institutions.

Applications may be submitted by, for example, institutions for visual arts, cultural heritage or design, municipalities, social and/or community organizations, such as (sports or retailers’) associations, schools, hospitals, churches, residents’ associations and foundations. Businesses, companies and individuals may also apply.

The applicant must be established in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.

The work to be commissioned must be accessible to the public and presented in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.

The work may not be for profit.

A realistic fee for the artist is mandatory, and must be included in the budget, in addition to the production costs.

The artist receiving the commission must have worked as a professional visual artist for at least 1 year: If the artist has completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on the diploma will be considered the start of their professional practice. If there is an interim period between graduation from the Bachelor’s programme with a visual arts curriculum and the start of a Master’s programme, this period will be considered as part of their professional practice. If the artist has not completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on which they first presented work in professional art circles will be considered the start of their professional practice.

The commissioned artist must be artistically active in the visual arts and in that capacity be embedded in the professional visual arts practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. For artists with a non-Dutch nationality, proof of registration in the Netherlands is also required.

If the project concerns a permanent work of art, it may not be moved or traded without permission of the Mondriaan Fund.",Art Commission,"Anyone without intention to sell the work can commission visual artists to create new works of art accessible to the public in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.

Anyone can apply, except for individual artists, art education institutions, post-graduate institutions and predominantly sales-oriented commercial art institutions.

Applications may be submitted by, for example, institutions for visual arts, cultural heritage or design, municipalities, social and/or community organizations, such as (sports or retailers’) associations, schools, hospitals, churches, residents’ associations and foundations. Businesses, companies and individuals may also apply.

The applicant must be established in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.

The work to be commissioned must be accessible to the public and presented in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.

The work may not be for profit.

A realistic fee for the artist is mandatory, and must be included in the budget, in addition to the production costs.

The artist receiving the commission must have worked as a professional visual artist for at least 1 year: If the artist has completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on the diploma will be considered the start of their professional practice. If there is an interim period between graduation from the Bachelor’s programme with a visual arts curriculum and the start of a Master’s programme, this period will be considered as part of their professional practice. If the artist has not completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on which they first presented work in professional art circles will be considered the start of their professional practice.

The commissioned artist must be artistically active in the visual arts and in that capacity be embedded in the professional visual arts practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. For artists with a non-Dutch nationality, proof of registration in the Netherlands is also required.

If the project concerns a permanent work of art, it may not be moved or traded without permission of the Mondriaan Fund.",Continuous,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.026824+00:00
mondriaan_fund_9c63efba31b9,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/art-fair-international/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,"Art Fair International grants strengthen the international standing of contemporary visual arts from the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom, and help it to become better known and appreciated.",visual arts,grant,Netherlands,,"The maximum grant depends on the percentage of work in the presentation by visual artists from the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom, and the cost of the (basic) stand rental.

Percentage of presented works by visual artists from the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom:
Less than 40%: grant is not available.
40% to 80%: 50% of the basic stand rental up to the maximum grant.
More than 80%: 80% of the basic stand rental up to the maximum grant.

Stand rental:
Less than € 20,000: maximum grant is € 4,750.
€ 20.000 to 30,000: maximum granti is € 6,750.
More than € 30,000: maximum grant is € 9,000.",,,en,Art Fair International,"For Dutch and non-Dutch galleries that subscribe to the Gallery Fair Practice Code, and publishers of art books.",Art Fair International,"For Dutch and non-Dutch galleries that subscribe to the Gallery Fair Practice Code, and publishers of art books.",Continuous,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.027176+00:00
mondriaan_fund_3324b2738f80,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/art-heritage-festival/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,"With the Art Heritage Festival grant, the Mondriaan Fund supports the presentation of visual art and/or heritage at festivals and similar events held in physical spaces that take place no more than once a year.",visual art and/or heritage,grant,Netherlands or Caribbean part of the Kingdom,,"The amount of the contribution is determined per application. The Mondriaan Fund can contribute up to 40% of the eligible project costs directly associated with the visual art and/or heritage activities for which the application is submitted. The minimum project budget must exceed € 25,000 and may only include costs directly related to the project. Grants of € 100,000 or more are highly exceptional.",,,en,Art Heritage Festival,Organisations based in the Netherlands or Caribbean part of the Kingdom that do not aim to generate profit or sales.,Art Heritage Festival,Organisations based in the Netherlands or Caribbean part of the Kingdom that do not aim to generate profit or sales.,Continuous,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.027541+00:00
mondriaan_fund_f452a1745b69,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/art-heritage-presentation/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,"With the Art Heritage Presentation grant, the Mondriaan Fund supports outstanding presentations by institutions working in the field of visual art and/or cultural heritage. The Fund provides grants for exhibitions and other forms of presentation that transcend the ordinary, engage the public in an appealing way, and are contextually relevant to contemporary visual art and/or cultural heritage in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.",visual art and/or cultural heritage,grant,Netherlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom,,The amount of the contribution is determined per application and is a maximum of 40% of the variable project costs.,,,en,Art Heritage Presentation,"This grant is intended for cultural institutions that focus on presenting cultural heritage and/or visual art. A cultural institution must be established in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom, and this must also be the location of the activities. Institutions for art education and post academic institutions are excluded from applying. The cultural institution is a legal entity or collective of legal entities, not aimed at generating profits or sales. Only presentations that are open to the public are eligible for funding. The activities may not be aimed at generating profit or sales. A grant is not available for festivals, biennales/triennales or similar events held once a year or less. Funding cannot be requested for publications, documentaries, symposia or conferences, unless they are an integral part of the presentation and serve as side programming, that is, a minor element of the presentation for which the primary application is submitted. All cultural institutions subscribe to the Fair Practice Code (Dutch only), the Culture Governance Code (Dutch only) and the Diversity & Inclusion Code (Dutch only). If an artist is involved with the plans, a realistic remuneration for the artist is obligatory and must be included in the budget. Artist’s fees are eligible for funding under the Art Heritage Presentation grant. If you have applied for the Art Heritage Presentation grant, you cannot simultaneously apply for the Artist’s Fee grant for the same project. Only if your application for the Art Heritage Presentation grant is rejected may you apply for the Artist’s Fee grant , provided the institution meets the eligibility criteria. Please also take into account the processing times of both grants and the start date of your project. In the budget, use one of these two calculators for your fair fee calculations. The project budget must also meet all requirements regarding fair pay. This means that everyone included in the budget must be paid in accordance with the applicable collective labour agreements or guidelines. This must be clearly detailed in both the application form and budget.",Art Heritage Presentation,"This grant is intended for cultural institutions that focus on presenting cultural heritage and/or visual art. A cultural institution must be established in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom, and this must also be the location of the activities. Institutions for art education and post academic institutions are excluded from applying. The cultural institution is a legal entity or collective of legal entities, not aimed at generating profits or sales. Only presentations that are open to the public are eligible for funding. The activities may not be aimed at generating profit or sales. A grant is not available for festivals, biennales/triennales or similar events held once a year or less. Funding cannot be requested for publications, documentaries, symposia or conferences, unless they are an integral part of the presentation and serve as side programming, that is, a minor element of the presentation for which the primary application is submitted. All cultural institutions subscribe to the Fair Practice Code (Dutch only), the Culture Governance Code (Dutch only) and the Diversity & Inclusion Code (Dutch only). If an artist is involved with the plans, a realistic remuneration for the artist is obligatory and must be included in the budget. Artist’s fees are eligible for funding under the Art Heritage Presentation grant. If you have applied for the Art Heritage Presentation grant, you cannot simultaneously apply for the Artist’s Fee grant for the same project. Only if your application for the Art Heritage Presentation grant is rejected may you apply for the Artist’s Fee grant , provided the institution meets the eligibility criteria. Please also take into account the processing times of both grants and the start date of your project. In the budget, use one of these two calculators for your fair fee calculations. The project budget must also meet all requirements regarding fair pay. This means that everyone included in the budget must be paid in accordance with the applicable collective labour agreements or guidelines. This must be clearly detailed in both the application form and budget.",Continuous,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.029966+00:00
mondriaan_fund_927ae2095ba6,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/artist-basic/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,"Artist Basic grant is for visual artists, to help them make new work and for the further development of their professional practice.",visual arts,grant,the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom,,"€ 50,000. This amount will be paid in segments over no less than 2 and no more than 4 years.",,,en,Artist Basic,Applications may only be submitted by artists who have been working as professional visual artists for at least 4 years:,Artist Basic,Applications may only be submitted by artists who have been working as professional visual artists for at least 4 years:,Continuous,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.030500+00:00
mondriaan_fund_a939eddff305,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/artist-project/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,The Mondriaan Fund offers Artist Project grants to stimulate talent development by providing visual artists the opportunity to realise an artistic plan that can significantly impact the quality and visibility of contemporary visual art in the Netherlands and/or Caribbean part of the Kingdom.,visual arts,grant,The Netherlands and/or Caribbean part of the Kingdom,,"Fixed contribution: A fixed contribution for no longer than 6 months. The standard amount is € 2.785,- per month. Flexible contribution: A flexible contribution for no longer than 12 months. The amount depends on the plan, the duration of the project and the budget.",,professionally active for at least 1 year,en,Artist Project,"Applications can only be submitted by visual artists who have been professionally active for at least 1 year: If you have completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on your diploma will be considered the start of your professional practice. If there is an interim period between your graduation from the Bachelor’s programme with a visual arts curriculum and the start of your Master’s programme, this period will be considered as part of your professional practice. If you have not completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on which you first presented work in professional art circles will be considered the start of your professional practice. In order to be eligible for a contribution, you must be artistically and substantively active within the visual arts field, and in this capacity, part of the professional art practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. You cannot apply for or use a contribution while enrolled to study at educational institutions for e.g. Bachelor’s, Master’s or postdoctoral programmes. This also applies to participation in programmes at postgraduate institutions and to PhD programmes. The exception is part-time programmes (not Bachelor’s programmes) of less than 20 hours a week.",Artist Project,"Applications can only be submitted by visual artists who have been professionally active for at least 1 year: If you have completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on your diploma will be considered the start of your professional practice. If there is an interim period between your graduation from the Bachelor’s programme with a visual arts curriculum and the start of your Master’s programme, this period will be considered as part of your professional practice. If you have not completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on which you first presented work in professional art circles will be considered the start of your professional practice. In order to be eligible for a contribution, you must be artistically and substantively active within the visual arts field, and in this capacity, part of the professional art practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. You cannot apply for or use a contribution while enrolled to study at educational institutions for e.g. Bachelor’s, Master’s or postdoctoral programmes. This also applies to participation in programmes at postgraduate institutions and to PhD programmes. The exception is part-time programmes (not Bachelor’s programmes) of less than 20 hours a week.",Continuous,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.031105+00:00
mondriaan_fund_bccb4029c0d9,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/artist-start/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,"The Mondriaan Fund offers Artist Start grants to stimulate the artistic development and cultural entrepreneurship of promising artists at the start of their careers, supporting the creation of work that can make a valuable contribution to contemporary visual art in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.",visual arts,grant,the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom,,"€ 24,900 for 12 months.",,artists at the start of their careers,en,Artist Start,"Artist Start grants are for visual artists who have been working professionally for at least 1 and no more than 4 years.

In order to be eligible for a contribution, you must be artistically active in the visual arts and in that capacity embedded in the professional visual arts practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom

Applications may only be submitted by artists who have been active as a professional visual artist for at least 1 year and no more than 4 years: If you have completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on your diploma will be considered the start of your professional practice. If there is an interim period between your graduation from the Bachelor’s programme with a visual arts curriculum and the start of your Master’s programme, this period will be considered as part of your professional practice. If you have not completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on which you first presented work in professional art circles will be considered the start of your professional practice. A period during which the applicant is enrolled for a Master’s degree programme does not count towards the duration of the professional practice. A period of enrolment in postdoctoral programmes and programmes at postgraduate institutions, such as the Rijksakademie, de Ateliers, the Jan van Eyck Academie, BAK or EKWC, will be counted as part of the duration of the professional practice. You cannot apply for or use a contribution while enrolled to study at educational institutions for e.g. Bachelor’s, Master’s or postdoctoral programmes. This also applies to participation in programmes at postgraduate institutions and to PhD programmes. The exception is part-time programmes (not Bachelor’s programmes) of less than 20 hours a week.

Previous applications: Only one Artist Start grant is awarded to any artists. An artist who was previously rejected on the grounds of the criterium ‘quality and development of the oeuvre’ is not permitted to submit a new application for Artist Start within a period of 12 months after the initial application date. An Artist Start grant may not be applied for during the term of any other financial support from the Mondriaan Fund if the board believes that the contribution could cover the same costs.

For the Artist Start grant, the applicant’s total taxable income in the period for which the application is submitted must not be higher than € 55,000.",Artist Start,"Artist Start grants are for visual artists who have been working professionally for at least 1 and no more than 4 years.

In order to be eligible for a contribution, you must be artistically active in the visual arts and in that capacity embedded in the professional visual arts practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom

Applications may only be submitted by artists who have been active as a professional visual artist for at least 1 year and no more than 4 years: If you have completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on your diploma will be considered the start of your professional practice. If there is an interim period between your graduation from the Bachelor’s programme with a visual arts curriculum and the start of your Master’s programme, this period will be considered as part of your professional practice. If you have not completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on which you first presented work in professional art circles will be considered the start of your professional practice. A period during which the applicant is enrolled for a Master’s degree programme does not count towards the duration of the professional practice. A period of enrolment in postdoctoral programmes and programmes at postgraduate institutions, such as the Rijksakademie, de Ateliers, the Jan van Eyck Academie, BAK or EKWC, will be counted as part of the duration of the professional practice. You cannot apply for or use a contribution while enrolled to study at educational institutions for e.g. Bachelor’s, Master’s or postdoctoral programmes. This also applies to participation in programmes at postgraduate institutions and to PhD programmes. The exception is part-time programmes (not Bachelor’s programmes) of less than 20 hours a week.

Previous applications: Only one Artist Start grant is awarded to any artists. An artist who was previously rejected on the grounds of the criterium ‘quality and development of the oeuvre’ is not permitted to submit a new application for Artist Start within a period of 12 months after the initial application date. An Artist Start grant may not be applied for during the term of any other financial support from the Mondriaan Fund if the board believes that the contribution could cover the same costs.

For the Artist Start grant, the applicant’s total taxable income in the period for which the application is submitted must not be higher than € 55,000.",Continuous,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.031728+00:00
mondriaan_fund_d73d8c3cb49e,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/artists-fee/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,Are you organising an exhibition as a visual arts institution and would you like a contribution towards the costs of the artist’s fee? And do you apply the guideline for artists’ fees? You may be eligible for an Artist’s Fee grant.,visual art,grant,the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom,,We determine the amount of the contribution per application.,,,en,Artist’s Fee,"The grant is intended for visual art institutions that exhibit contemporary visual art and/or heritage by artists from home or abroad without a sales purpose.

If the applicant is a publicly accessible visual arts institution established in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom whose core activity is to exhibit contemporary visual art and/or heritage without a sales objective.

If the visual arts institution applies fair pay and signs an agreement to this effect, and also has it signed by the artist(s).

When the artist receiving the fee has at least a bachelor’s degree in visual arts or has worked as a professional visual artist for 3 years or more.

If the amount of the fee is at least equal to the amount proposed in the guideline.

When the application has been submitted at least 2 months before the start of the exhibition.

When the exhibition opens to the public within 12 months of submitting the application.

When you pay the invoices of the visual artist(s) within 1 month of the invoice date.

Applicants subscribe to the Fair Practice Code (in Dutch) , Culture Governance Code (in Dutch) and the Diversity & Inclusion Code (in Dutch) .

An application for a contribution of less than €100 will not be processed.

For activities taking place in 2025-2028, no contribution can be made to:

Institutions that receive multi-year support under the Art Platform Programmes 2025-2028 grant;
Institutions that will receive multi-year support in 2025-2028 from one of the other National Culture Funds;
Institutions that are part of the basic cultural infrastructure 2025-2028 (bis), with the exception of regional museums, provided that they do not already receive a subsidy for the relevant activities under the Regulation on specific cultural policy;
Institutions that are supported on the basis of the National Collection Management and Subsidies for Museum Institutions Regulations (Heritage Act);
Institutions that have been awarded an Art Heritage Festival grant , Art Commission grant or an Art Heritage Presentation grant for the activity in question;
Institutions that otherwise receive funds for fair pay from the Ministry of Education, Culture and Science.",Artist’s Fee,"The grant is intended for visual art institutions that exhibit contemporary visual art and/or heritage by artists from home or abroad without a sales purpose.

If the applicant is a publicly accessible visual arts institution established in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom whose core activity is to exhibit contemporary visual art and/or heritage without a sales objective.

If the visual arts institution applies fair pay and signs an agreement to this effect, and also has it signed by the artist(s).

When the artist receiving the fee has at least a bachelor’s degree in visual arts or has worked as a professional visual artist for 3 years or more.

If the amount of the fee is at least equal to the amount proposed in the guideline.

When the application has been submitted at least 2 months before the start of the exhibition.

When the exhibition opens to the public within 12 months of submitting the application.

When you pay the invoices of the visual artist(s) within 1 month of the invoice date.

Applicants subscribe to the Fair Practice Code (in Dutch) , Culture Governance Code (in Dutch) and the Diversity & Inclusion Code (in Dutch) .

An application for a contribution of less than €100 will not be processed.

For activities taking place in 2025-2028, no contribution can be made to:

Institutions that receive multi-year support under the Art Platform Programmes 2025-2028 grant;
Institutions that will receive multi-year support in 2025-2028 from one of the other National Culture Funds;
Institutions that are part of the basic cultural infrastructure 2025-2028 (bis), with the exception of regional museums, provided that they do not already receive a subsidy for the relevant activities under the Regulation on specific cultural policy;
Institutions that are supported on the basis of the National Collection Management and Subsidies for Museum Institutions Regulations (Heritage Act);
Institutions that have been awarded an Art Heritage Festival grant , Art Commission grant or an Art Heritage Presentation grant for the activity in question;
Institutions that otherwise receive funds for fair pay from the Ministry of Education, Culture and Science.",Continuous,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.032117+00:00
mondriaan_fund_4518b4e5d09e,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/collection-mobility/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,"Do you represent a museum or other cultural heritage institution? Are you interested in selecting, discarding or relocating parts of a collection in order to improve the quality of the collection, make it more visible to the public, and improve the focus of the collection profile? If so, your institution may be eligible for a Collection Mobility grant.",museum collections / cultural heritage,grant,Dutch,,The amount of Collection Mobility will be determined for each individual application. The Mondriaan Fund will finance up to 40% of the eligible costs.,,,en,Collection Mobility,"Applications can be submitted by publicly accessible Dutch institutions that manage museum collections of national and international significance. If there is a receiving institution, the institutions must submit the application jointly. The applicants must be registered with the Dutch Museum Register. The applicant institutions must be accommodating in respect of the loan transactions with Dutch institutions and act in accordance with the Basic Principles for Smarter Loan Transactions in the Netherlands (Slimmer Lenen Uitgangspunten bruikleenverkeer binnen Nederland). This means that Dutch museums will not be charged expenses for loaning works of art and that direct costs such as transport, insurance and packaging expenses (handling fee) will be minimised. Collections must be disposed of in accordance with the Guideline for the Disposal of Museum Objects and, where possible, according to the valuation framework of the Dutch Cultural Heritage Agency. Applicants are expected to make a significant financial contribution themselves.",Collection Mobility,"Applications can be submitted by publicly accessible Dutch institutions that manage museum collections of national and international significance. If there is a receiving institution, the institutions must submit the application jointly. The applicants must be registered with the Dutch Museum Register. The applicant institutions must be accommodating in respect of the loan transactions with Dutch institutions and act in accordance with the Basic Principles for Smarter Loan Transactions in the Netherlands (Slimmer Lenen Uitgangspunten bruikleenverkeer binnen Nederland). This means that Dutch museums will not be charged expenses for loaning works of art and that direct costs such as transport, insurance and packaging expenses (handling fee) will be minimised. Collections must be disposed of in accordance with the Guideline for the Disposal of Museum Objects and, where possible, according to the valuation framework of the Dutch Cultural Heritage Agency. Applicants are expected to make a significant financial contribution themselves.",Continuous,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.032468+00:00
mondriaan_fund_3b86b5d4af2f,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/curator-researcher/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,"Are you an independent curator or art observer interested in conducting preliminary research for an exhibition, event, article or a presentation? For example, research into a theme, or through travel or a working period in the Netherlands or abroad? Would you like to work on a concrete plan in a defined period? If so, you may be eligible for the Curator Researcher grant.",visual arts and/or cultural heritage,grant,the Netherlands and/or Caribbean part of the Kingdom,,"A contribution of € 2,480 per month, for no more than 6 months.",,,en,Curator Researcher,"Independent curators, critics, theorists and art observers who have been professionally active for at least 2 years.

You have been working as a professional curator or art observer in the visual arts or cultural heritage field for at least 2 years and can demonstrate this with publications, exhibitions, research and/or other projects. You␀are artistically and substantively active within the visual arts and/or cultural heritage field, and in this capacity, part of the professional art and/or cultural heritage practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.

The Curator Researcher grant cannot be used to finance study. It is also not permitted to use the grant while enrolled to study at educational institutions for e.g. Bachelors, Masters or postdoctoral programmes. This also applies to participation in programmes at postgraduate institutions. The contribution is not intended for work on behalf of an organisation or for regular work. The contribution may not be used for a working period in a guest studio in the Netherlands or abroad if this studio is offered in the Mondriaan Funds Residency programme. The contribution may not be used for production, such as of a publication or exhibition, for (cultural-) historical research or organisational archival research.

At␀the time of submitting the application, you must not be receiving any other financial contribution from the Mondriaan Fund which, in the opinion of the board of the Mondriaan Fund, would cover the same costs. A curator or art observer can be awarded a contribution to cover time investment for no more than 24 months within a period of 48 months. A curator or art observer who is rejected on the grounds of the criterion quality and development of working practice is not permitted to submit a new application within a period of 12 months after the initial application.",Curator Researcher,"Independent curators, critics, theorists and art observers who have been professionally active for at least 2 years.

You have been working as a professional curator or art observer in the visual arts or cultural heritage field for at least 2 years and can demonstrate this with publications, exhibitions, research and/or other projects. You␀are artistically and substantively active within the visual arts and/or cultural heritage field, and in this capacity, part of the professional art and/or cultural heritage practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.

The Curator Researcher grant cannot be used to finance study. It is also not permitted to use the grant while enrolled to study at educational institutions for e.g. Bachelors, Masters or postdoctoral programmes. This also applies to participation in programmes at postgraduate institutions. The contribution is not intended for work on behalf of an organisation or for regular work. The contribution may not be used for a working period in a guest studio in the Netherlands or abroad if this studio is offered in the Mondriaan Funds Residency programme. The contribution may not be used for production, such as of a publication or exhibition, for (cultural-) historical research or organisational archival research.

At␀the time of submitting the application, you must not be receiving any other financial contribution from the Mondriaan Fund which, in the opinion of the board of the Mondriaan Fund, would cover the same costs. A curator or art observer can be awarded a contribution to cover time investment for no more than 24 months within a period of 48 months. A curator or art observer who is rejected on the grounds of the criterion quality and development of working practice is not permitted to submit a new application within a period of 12 months after the initial application.",Continuous,,2026-09-23 12:37:34.032817+00:00
mondriaan_fund_6d9761361246,mondriaan_fund,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/international-art-presentation/,https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/login/,Mondriaan Fund,"Are you an artist and are you going to present your work abroad? Or do you, as an internationally recognised art institution, want to show contemporary art from the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom abroad, possibly in combination with new work to be made? You may be eligible for an International Art Presentation contribution.",visual arts,grant,the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom,,"How much? Travel costs (return) for the artist(s) and/or (guest) curator for a single production trip and a single trip to be present at the opening of the presentation; A maximum of € 1000 per person for the participating artists and/or guest curators from the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom, towards lodging; Transport and insurance expenses during transport of the work being presented; A maximum of 50% of the production costs of new (site-specific) work commissioned by the non-Dutch art institution; A maximum of 25% of costs of the publication associated with the presentation; A maximum of 50% of the translation costs of subtitling a film.",,professional visual artist,en,International Art Presentation,"Artists who are artistically active in the visual arts and in that capacity are embedded in the professional contemporary visual arts practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom (Aruba, Bonaire, Curaçao, Saba, Sint Maarten and Sint Eustatius) who want to present work abroad, or internationally recognised art institutions outside the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom that want to show current work by living visual artists from the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom can receive a contribution.

If you have to make a financial contribution to participate in the presentation, you are not eligible for a contribution under this grant. In order to be eligible for a contribution, you must be artistically and substantively active within the visual arts field, and in that capacity are embedded in the professional contemporary visual arts practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. Applications may only be submitted by artists who have been working as a professional visual artist for at least 1 year.

If the application relates to the production of new work, the international institution is expected to include a realistic fee for the artist in the budget, with an explanation of how the amount of the fee was determined. This cost item falls under production costs, but must be paid by the institution to the artist and/or guest curator.

If your exhibition takes place at a commercial gallery, you are not eligible for an International Art Presentation contribution.

A contribution can only be made for presentations by living artists who are artistically active in the visual arts and in that capacity are embedded in the professional contemporary visual arts practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.

The artist whose work is being displayed must have worked as a professional visual artist for at least 1 year:

If the artist has completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on the diploma will be considered the start of their professional practice. If there is an interim period between graduation from the Bachelor’s programme with a visual arts curriculum and the start of a Master’s programme, this period will be considered as part of their professional practice. If the artist has not completed a Bachelor’s degree programme (HBO) with a visual arts curriculum, the date on which they first presented work in professional art circles will be considered the start of their professional practice.

The presenting institution is an internationally recognised art institution outside the Netherlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom whose main goal is to show contemporary art, and is therefore not primarily focused on sales. As an exception, a foreign art institution can request a contribution to show work by master students in a visual arts programme or participants in post-academic institutions.

If a foreign institution involves a guest curator from the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom in the project, then he or she has been professionally active as a curator in the field of contempora",International Art Presentation,"Artists who are artistically active in the visual arts and in that capacity are embedded in the professional contemporary visual arts practice in the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom (Aruba, Bonaire, Curaçao, Saba, Sint Maarten and Sint Eustatius) who want to present work abroad, or internationally recognised art institutions outside the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom that want to show current work by living visual artists from the Netherlands and/or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom can receive a contribution.

